window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":1,"qs":[{"id":"E1B-12","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"AWS Batch with Spot","q":"A research company runs containerized image-processing jobs that each take 2 to 6 hours. Thousands of jobs are submitted every week in bursts. The jobs are checkpointed and can be retried if interrupted. The company wants to minimize compute costs and avoid managing job queues or scheduling logic. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run each job as an AWS Lambda function using a container image.","Use AWS Batch with a managed compute environment that uses EC2 Spot Instances and a job queue.","Run the containers as an Amazon ECS service on AWS Fargate with On-Demand capacity that is always running.","Launch Reserved Instances in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group and schedule jobs with cron."],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah durasi '2 to 6 hours', beban yang datang 'in bursts', job yang 'can be retried if interrupted', dan keinginan untuk 'minimize compute costs' tanpa mengelola antrean atau penjadwalan. AWS Batch menyediakan job queue, scheduler, dan managed compute environment yang menskalakan kapasitas sesuai jumlah job, termasuk ke nol saat idle; memakai Spot Instance sangat cocok karena job toleran interupsi dan bisa di-retry. Lambda adalah distraktor yang gagal karena batas 15 menit. ECS service Fargate yang selalu menyala membayar kapasitas terus-menerus padahal beban datang bergelombang. Reserved Instance dengan cron membayar kapasitas tetap dan menuntut logika penjadwalan sendiri. Aturan umum: batch container jangka panjang, bursty, dan toleran interupsi → AWS Batch + Spot.","r":["Salah — Lambda dibatasi 15 menit per invocation sehingga job 2–6 jam tidak bisa berjalan.","Benar — AWS Batch mengelola antrean, penjadwalan, dan scaling; Spot menekan biaya untuk job yang bisa di-retry.","Salah — Service yang selalu berjalan membayar kapasitas walau tidak ada job; On-Demand juga lebih mahal daripada Spot.","Salah — Reserved Instance membayar kapasitas tetap untuk beban bursty dan cron berarti mengelola penjadwalan sendiri."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'long-running batch containers + queue + cost + interruptible' → AWS Batch dengan Spot."},{"id":"E2B-12","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler S3 event mode","q":"A data engineer must run AWS Glue crawlers on an S3 bucket that receives new objects at unpredictable times throughout the day in existing and new prefixes. The catalog must reflect new data within minutes, and the crawler must not list the full bucket on every run because the bucket contains more than 50 million objects. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","o":["Schedule the crawler to run every 5 minutes with the default recrawl policy.","Configure an S3 Event Notification to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the CreatePartition API for every object.","Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to start a full crawl whenever any object is uploaded.","Configure S3 Event Notifications to an Amazon SQS queue and set the crawler to use S3 event mode so it crawls only the changed objects."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'unpredictable times', 'existing and new prefixes', 'within minutes' dan 'must not list the full bucket'. Crawler dengan S3 event mode membaca event dari antrean SQS yang menerima S3 Event Notifications, lalu hanya memproses objek/folder yang berubah. Ini menangani file baru di prefix lama maupun baru tanpa listing 50 juta objek, sehingga cepat dan murah. Full crawl tiap 5 menit atau di setiap upload sangat mahal dan run-nya bisa saling bertumpuk. Lambda yang memanggil CreatePartition untuk setiap objek adalah kode kustom, menghasilkan banyak panggilan API untuk partisi yang sama, dan tidak menangani perubahan skema. Ingat: crawler + bucket besar + data tiba acak → S3 event mode dengan SQS; append folder terjadwal → crawl new folders only.","r":["Salah — Full crawl tiap 5 menit melisting seluruh bucket, sehingga biaya dan durasinya besar.","Salah — Lambda per objek adalah kode kustom, menghasilkan panggilan API berulang, dan tidak mendeteksi perubahan skema.","Salah — Full crawl per upload sangat mahal dan menghasilkan run yang tumpang tindih.","Benar — S3 event mode memproses hanya objek yang berubah dari antrean SQS, cepat dan hemat."],"k":"Tips ujian: crawler 'event-driven' / 'avoid full listing' → S3 Event Notifications → SQS → crawler S3 event mode."},{"id":"E4B-25","d":4,"ts":"4.4.1","t":"CloudTrail organization trail and integrity validation","q":"A company uses AWS Organizations with 60 member accounts that run data pipelines. The audit team requires that API activity from all current and future accounts be collected in one central location that member account administrators cannot modify, and that auditors be able to prove the log files were not altered after delivery. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an organization trail in the management account (or delegated administrator account) that delivers logs to an S3 bucket in a dedicated log archive account.","Create an individual trail in each member account that sends events to a CloudWatch Logs log group in the same account.","Enable CloudTrail Insights on the trail.","Configure an S3 Lifecycle rule that moves the log files to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 30 days.","Enable CloudTrail log file integrity validation on the trail."],"a":[0,4],"e":"Ada dua syarat: log terpusat dari 'all current and future accounts' yang 'cannot modify' oleh admin member, dan bukti bahwa log 'were not altered after delivery'. Organization trail dibuat sekali di management account (atau delegated administrator) dan otomatis berlaku untuk semua akun anggota, termasuk akun baru; member account dapat melihat trail tersebut tetapi tidak dapat mengubah atau menghapusnya. Log disimpan di bucket pada log archive account yang terpisah. Log file integrity validation menghasilkan digest file (SHA-256 dengan tanda tangan digital) setiap jam sehingga auditor dapat memverifikasi bahwa file log tidak diubah atau dihapus. Distraktor terdekat adalah trail per akun: admin akun bisa menghapusnya, akun baru tidak otomatis tercakup, dan log tidak terpusat. CloudTrail Insights mendeteksi aktivitas API yang tidak biasa, bukan integritas file. Lifecycle ke Glacier mengurangi biaya, bukan membuktikan integritas. Aturan umum: audit multi-akun → organization trail + bucket di log archive account + log file integrity validation.","r":["Benar — Organization trail mencakup semua akun saat ini dan yang akan datang, dan tidak dapat diubah oleh member account.","Salah — Trail per akun dapat diubah admin lokal, tidak terpusat, dan tidak otomatis mencakup akun baru.","Salah — Insights mendeteksi anomali volume/error API, bukan memastikan integritas file log.","Salah — Lifecycle ke Glacier menghemat biaya penyimpanan, tidak membuktikan log tidak diubah.","Benar — Integrity validation menghasilkan digest file untuk membuktikan log tidak dimodifikasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'prove logs not tampered' → log file integrity validation; 'all accounts incl. future' → organization trail."},{"id":"E4B-01","d":4,"ts":"4.3.1","t":"Redshift dynamic data masking","q":"A retail company stores customer payment data in an Amazon Redshift table. Business analysts must see only the last four digits of the credit_card column, while the fraud investigation team must see the full value. The company does not want to duplicate data or maintain separate tables or views for each team. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create one view for analysts that uses a SUBSTRING expression and another view for the fraud team, and grant each team SELECT on its own view only.","Create a Redshift dynamic data masking policy that shows only the last four digits, and attach it to the credit_card column for the analyst role while the fraud team role keeps an unmasked policy.","Run a nightly AWS Glue job that writes a masked copy of the table for analysts and keep the original table for the fraud team.","Enable Amazon Macie on the Redshift cluster to detect credit card numbers and mask them automatically for analysts."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'does not want to duplicate data or maintain separate tables or views' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon Redshift dynamic data masking (DDM) memungkinkan Anda membuat masking policy (misalnya hanya menampilkan 4 digit terakhir) lalu meng-attach policy tersebut ke kolom untuk role/user tertentu. Masking terjadi saat query dijalankan, sehingga data asli tidak diduplikasi dan tidak ada objek tambahan per tim yang perlu dirawat. Fraud team dapat diberi policy dengan prioritas lebih tinggi yang tidak melakukan masking. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat view per tim: secara fungsional bisa, tetapi justru melanggar syarat 'tidak memelihara view per tim' dan sulit diskalakan saat tim bertambah. Glue job membuat salinan data (duplikasi + biaya + data basi). Macie hanya mendeteksi data sensitif di Amazon S3, tidak memasking data di Redshift. Aturan umum: masking per role di Redshift tanpa duplikasi → Redshift dynamic data masking.","r":["Salah — View per tim memang bisa menyembunyikan digit, tetapi menambah objek yang harus dipelihara per tim, bertentangan dengan constraint soal.","Benar — DDM menerapkan masking saat query berdasarkan role, tanpa salinan data dan tanpa view per tim.","Salah — Membuat salinan ter-masking berarti duplikasi data, biaya tambahan, dan data analis tertinggal hingga job berikutnya.","Salah — Macie menganalisis objek di Amazon S3 dan tidak melakukan masking kolom di Redshift."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'mask column per role/user in Redshift, no copies' → Redshift dynamic data masking (CREATE MASKING POLICY + ATTACH ... TO ROLE)."},{"id":"E2C-24","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"DMS Schema Conversion generative AI conversion","q":"A data engineer is using AWS DMS Schema Conversion to convert an Oracle schema to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. The assessment shows that several complex PL/SQL packages cannot be fully converted by the rule-based engine. The team wants to reduce the amount of manual rewriting while still reviewing the results before applying them. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Use the generative AI conversion option in DMS Schema Conversion for the objects that the rules cannot fully convert, review the converted code, and then apply it.","Skip the packages and rely on AWS DMS CDC to replicate the procedure logic.","Convert the packages into AWS Glue jobs automatically by using a Glue crawler.","Change the target to Amazon DynamoDB so that stored procedures are not needed."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah objek PL/SQL kompleks yang 'cannot be fully converted by the rule-based engine' dan keinginan mengurangi penulisan ulang manual sambil tetap me-review. DMS Schema Conversion memakai engine berbasis aturan, dan untuk jalur tertentu seperti Oracle ke Aurora/RDS PostgreSQL tersedia opsi konversi generative AI yang mencoba mengonversi lebih banyak objek yang gagal dikonversi aturan. Hasilnya tetap harus di-review lalu diterapkan ke target atau diekspor sebagai skrip SQL. DMS CDC hanya mereplikasi perubahan data, bukan logika stored procedure. Glue crawler hanya membuat metadata katalog dan tidak mengubah PL/SQL menjadi job. Mengganti target ke DynamoDB mengubah arsitektur aplikasi secara besar dan tidak relevan. Aturan umum: sisa objek kode yang gagal dikonversi otomatis → generative AI conversion di DMS Schema Conversion, lalu review manual.","r":["Benar — Konversi generative AI di DMS Schema Conversion mengurangi pekerjaan manual untuk objek yang gagal dikonversi aturan, dengan review sebelum apply.","Salah — CDC mereplikasi data, bukan logika stored procedure.","Salah — Glue crawler tidak mengonversi kode PL/SQL.","Salah — Mengganti target ke DynamoDB adalah redesign besar dan tidak menyelesaikan kebutuhan konversi."],"k":"Tips ujian: objek kode kompleks yang tidak terkonversi oleh rules → DMS Schema Conversion generative AI conversion + review."},{"id":"E2B-24","d":2,"ts":"2.2.5","t":"Glue target connection to Redshift","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job must load transformed data into an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster that runs in private subnets. The job should use the Glue Redshift integration so that data is staged in Amazon S3 and loaded with the COPY command instead of row-by-row inserts. Which configuration meets these requirements?","o":["Use the Amazon Redshift Data API from a Python shell job to INSERT each row into the target table.","Make the Redshift cluster publicly accessible and connect to it from the Glue job without a Glue connection.","Use an AWS Glue crawler to write the data into Redshift tables.","Create an AWS Glue connection of type Amazon Redshift in the cluster's VPC, use it as the job's target, and specify an S3 temporary directory and an IAM role that Redshift can use to read it."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'private subnets', 'Glue Redshift integration' dan 'staged in Amazon S3 and loaded with the COPY command'. Untuk target Redshift, Glue memakai connection bertipe Amazon Redshift (JDBC) di VPC cluster sehingga job bisa menjangkau endpoint privat. Konektor Redshift di Glue menulis data ke S3 temporary directory (redshiftTmpDir) lalu menjalankan COPY dengan IAM role yang diizinkan membaca bucket itu, jauh lebih cepat daripada insert per baris. Data API dengan INSERT per baris lambat dan mahal untuk volume besar. Membuat cluster publik melanggar desain jaringan privat. Crawler hanya membaca metadata, bukan menulis data. Ingat: Glue → Redshift = Redshift connection + temp dir S3 + IAM role untuk COPY.","r":["Salah — INSERT per baris lewat Data API sangat lambat untuk load massal dan bukan COPY.","Salah — Membuka cluster ke publik melanggar desain jaringan privat dan tidak perlu.","Salah — Crawler hanya membuat metadata catalog, tidak memuat data ke Redshift.","Benar — Redshift connection di VPC + temp dir S3 + IAM role memungkinkan Glue memuat data dengan COPY."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue job target Redshift → Glue connection Redshift + redshiftTmpDir + IAM role (COPY di belakang layar)."},{"id":"E1B-36","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"Choosing Lambda vs Glue for cost","q":"A company receives about 2,000 small CSV files (each under 1 MB) per day at random times in Amazon S3. Each file needs a simple column mapping and must be written as JSON to another prefix. Processing currently uses an AWS Glue Spark job that is triggered for every file, and the Glue bill is much higher than expected. Which solution will MOST reduce cost while preserving per-file processing?","o":["Increase the number of Glue workers so that each run finishes faster.","Switch the Glue job to the G.2X worker type.","Batch the files and run the Glue job once per week.","Replace the Glue job with an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by S3 event notifications for each file."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah 'about 2,000 small CSV files' di bawah 1 MB, transformasi 'simple column mapping', pemrosesan per file, dan tagihan Glue yang tinggi. Setiap run Glue Spark memiliki waktu startup dan minimum billing per run serta kapasitas minimal beberapa DPU, sehingga menjalankannya ribuan kali per hari untuk file kecil sangat boros. Lambda ditagih per milidetik dan per invocation, cocok untuk transformasi ringan per file yang selesai dalam detik. Menambah worker atau memakai G.2X justru menaikkan biaya. Batch mingguan menghemat biaya, tetapi menghilangkan pemrosesan per file dan menunda data. Aturan umum: banyak file kecil dengan transformasi ringan → Lambda; data besar → Glue/EMR.","r":["Salah — Lebih banyak worker menambah DPU yang ditagih tanpa mengatasi overhead per run.","Salah — Worker lebih besar berarti biaya per jam lebih tinggi.","Salah — Mengubah pemrosesan per file menjadi mingguan dan menunda data secara signifikan.","Benar — Lambda per file sangat murah untuk transformasi ringan dan tetap event-driven."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'many tiny files + simple transform + Glue too expensive' → Lambda (pay per ms), bukan Spark."},{"id":"E1A-05","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"AWS DMS CDC to Kinesis","q":"A company runs an on-premises Oracle database that records financial transactions. The company needs to stream every insert, update, and delete into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams in near real time, after first loading the existing data. The solution must not require changes to the application code. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use AWS DataSync to copy the Oracle data files to Amazon S3 every 5 minutes.","Create an AWS DMS task of type full load and CDC with the Oracle database as the source endpoint and the Kinesis data stream as the target endpoint.","Create an AWS Glue crawler on the Oracle database and run it every minute.","Use AWS Transfer Family to export the Oracle redo logs to Amazon S3.","Enable supplemental logging on the Oracle source database so that AWS DMS can capture changes."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'existing data' lalu 'every insert, update, and delete' secara 'near real time' tanpa mengubah aplikasi. AWS DMS dengan tipe task full load and CDC memuat data awal lalu terus mereplikasi perubahan, dan Kinesis Data Streams didukung sebagai target endpoint. Agar DMS bisa membaca perubahan dari redo log Oracle, supplemental logging harus diaktifkan di database sumber. DataSync hanya menyalin file, bukan perubahan tingkat baris yang konsisten dari database yang sedang berjalan. Glue crawler hanya membaca metadata/skema, bukan perubahan data. Transfer Family adalah layanan SFTP/FTPS, bukan CDC. Aturan umum: CDC dari database relasional ke stream tanpa ubah aplikasi = DMS full load + CDC, dengan prasyarat logging sumber (supplemental logging di Oracle, binlog di MySQL).","r":["Salah — DataSync menyalin file, bukan perubahan baris; menyalin datafile database yang aktif tidak menghasilkan CDC.","Benar — DMS full load and CDC memuat data awal lalu mereplikasi perubahan ke Kinesis Data Streams sebagai target.","Salah — Glue crawler hanya mendeteksi skema/metadata, tidak menangkap perubahan data.","Salah — Transfer Family adalah layanan transfer file SFTP/FTPS, bukan solusi CDC.","Benar — Supplemental logging di Oracle diperlukan agar DMS dapat menangkap perubahan (CDC) dari redo log."],"k":"Database → stream perubahan tanpa ubah kode → AWS DMS full load + CDC (Oracle: aktifkan supplemental logging)."},{"id":"E1A-47","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Kinesis enhanced fan-out with Lambda","q":"A Kinesis data stream has four consumer applications that use shared-throughput polling, and each shard's 2 MB/s read limit is already saturated. A new latency-sensitive AWS Lambda function must consume the same stream with its own dedicated read throughput, without affecting the existing consumers. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Have the Lambda function call GetRecords in a loop more frequently.","Increase the Lambda function's reserved concurrency.","Set the event source mapping batch size to 10,000 records.","Register the Lambda function as an enhanced fan-out consumer of the stream and use the consumer ARN in the event source mapping."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: batas baca 2 MB/s per shard 'already saturated' oleh consumer bersama, consumer baru butuh 'dedicated read throughput' dan 'latency-sensitive'. Enhanced fan-out (EFO) memberi setiap consumer yang terdaftar throughput khusus 2 MB/s per shard dengan push melalui HTTP/2 (SubscribeToShard), sehingga tidak berbagi kuota dengan consumer standar dan latensinya lebih rendah. Lambda mendukung EFO dengan menunjuk consumer ARN pada event source mapping. Distraktor terdekat adalah memanggil GetRecords lebih sering: justru memperparah pelanggaran batas 5 panggilan per detik per shard dan 2 MB/s bersama. Reserved concurrency dan batch size tidak menambah throughput baca shard. Aturan umum: banyak consumer pada Kinesis atau butuh latensi rendah = enhanced fan-out.","r":["Salah — Polling lebih sering memperburuk throttling pada kuota baca bersama.","Salah — Concurrency tidak menambah throughput baca shard yang sudah jenuh.","Salah — Batch size lebih besar tidak menambah kuota baca bersama per shard.","Benar — EFO memberi throughput baca khusus per consumer dan latensi rendah tanpa mengganggu consumer lain."],"k":"Kinesis read limit jenuh / consumer butuh throughput khusus → enhanced fan-out (consumer ARN di Lambda ESM)."},{"id":"E2B-36","d":2,"ts":"2.3.2","t":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering","q":"A data lake stores 300 TB of Parquet files in Amazon S3. Some datasets are read heavily for a few weeks and then never again, while others become popular again months later. Access patterns cannot be predicted per dataset, and the team does not want to pay retrieval fees when cold data is suddenly read. Which storage approach is MOST cost-effective with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create Lifecycle rules that move all objects to S3 Standard-IA after 30 days.","Keep all data in S3 Standard and review access logs monthly to move datasets manually.","Create Lifecycle rules that move all objects to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval after 30 days.","Store the data in S3 Intelligent-Tiering so that objects move automatically between access tiers based on access patterns."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'access patterns cannot be predicted', 'become popular again months later' dan 'not ... pay retrieval fees'. S3 Intelligent-Tiering memantau akses per objek dan otomatis memindahkannya antara tier Frequent, Infrequent dan Archive Instant Access, lalu mengembalikannya ke Frequent saat diakses, tanpa biaya retrieval (hanya biaya monitoring kecil per objek). Lifecycle rule ke Standard-IA atau Glacier Instant Retrieval berbasis umur, sehingga dataset yang kembali populer akan dikenai biaya retrieval per GB yang besar. Review manual bulanan adalah overhead tinggi dan reaktif. Ingat: akses tidak terprediksi + tanpa retrieval fee → S3 Intelligent-Tiering; akses yang terprediksi menurut umur → Lifecycle transitions.","r":["Salah — Data yang kembali populer di Standard-IA dikenai retrieval fee, dan aturan berbasis umur tidak cocok untuk akses tidak terduga.","Salah — Pemindahan manual adalah overhead operasional tinggi dan rawan terlambat.","Salah — Glacier Instant Retrieval punya retrieval fee yang lebih tinggi untuk data yang tiba-tiba sering dibaca.","Benar — Intelligent-Tiering mengoptimalkan biaya otomatis sesuai akses tanpa retrieval fee."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'unknown/changing access patterns' → S3 Intelligent-Tiering."},{"id":"E1C-64","d":1,"ts":"1.4.5","t":"CloudFormation change sets and retention policies","q":"A production AWS CloudFormation stack contains an Amazon Redshift cluster and an Amazon S3 bucket with critical data. A data engineer must update the stack template. The engineer wants to know before the update whether any resource will be replaced, and wants to ensure that the data in these resources is preserved even if they are replaced or removed from the template. Which combination of actions should the engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a change set for the stack and review the proposed changes, including the Replacement field, before executing it.","Run drift detection on the stack before updating it.","Set DeletionPolicy and UpdateReplacePolicy to Retain (or Snapshot where supported) on the Redshift cluster and the S3 bucket.","Enable termination protection on the stack.","Delete the stack and create a new stack from the updated template."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Dua kebutuhan: tahu 'before the update whether any resource will be replaced', dan data 'preserved even if they are replaced or removed'. Change set menampilkan perubahan yang akan dilakukan, termasuk apakah setiap resource akan diganti (Replacement: True/False/Conditional), sebelum dieksekusi. DeletionPolicy menentukan perlakuan saat resource dihapus dari template atau stack dihapus, dan UpdateReplacePolicy menentukan perlakuan terhadap resource lama saat diganti; nilai Retain atau Snapshot (untuk Redshift) menjaga data. Distractor terdekat adalah termination protection: hanya mencegah penghapusan seluruh stack, bukan penggantian resource saat update. Drift detection membandingkan konfigurasi aktual dengan template, bukan pratinjau update. Menghapus stack justru berisiko kehilangan data. Aturan umum: pratinjau perubahan → change set; lindungi resource stateful → DeletionPolicy/UpdateReplacePolicy Retain atau Snapshot.","r":["Benar — Change set menunjukkan resource mana yang akan dimodifikasi atau diganti sebelum update dijalankan.","Salah — Drift detection mendeteksi perubahan manual, bukan pratinjau perubahan template.","Benar — Kebijakan Retain/Snapshot menjaga data saat resource diganti atau dihapus.","Salah — Termination protection hanya mencegah penghapusan stack, bukan penggantian resource.","Salah — Menghapus stack berisiko menghapus resource beserta datanya."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'preview changes' → change set; 'keep data on replace/delete' → UpdateReplacePolicy/DeletionPolicy Retain."},{"id":"E4B-49","d":4,"ts":"4.5.4","t":"AWS Config configuration history","q":"During a compliance review, an auditor asks a data engineer to show exactly what the bucket policy and default encryption settings of an S3 bucket that holds financial data looked like 2 weeks ago, and how they have changed since then. Which AWS service should the data engineer use?","o":["Amazon CloudWatch metrics for Amazon S3","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS Config configuration history (resource timeline) for the bucket","Amazon S3 server access logs"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'exactly what the bucket policy and default encryption settings ... looked like 2 weeks ago, and how they have changed'. AWS Config merekam configuration item setiap kali konfigurasi resource berubah, sehingga resource timeline menunjukkan kondisi konfigurasi pada titik waktu tertentu beserta perbedaan antar versi. Timeline Config juga menautkan event CloudTrail terkait, sehingga perubahan dapat dikorelasikan dengan siapa yang melakukannya. Distraktor terdekat adalah S3 server access logs: mencatat request ke bucket, tetapi tidak menyimpan snapshot konfigurasi bucket policy dan enkripsi. CloudWatch metrics berisi angka penggunaan seperti jumlah request dan ukuran bucket. Trusted Advisor memberi rekomendasi best practice pada kondisi saat ini, bukan histori konfigurasi. Aturan umum: 'what did the configuration look like at time X / history of changes' → AWS Config; 'who called the API' → CloudTrail.","r":["Salah — Metrics hanya berisi data numerik penggunaan, bukan isi konfigurasi.","Salah — Trusted Advisor memeriksa kondisi saat ini untuk rekomendasi, bukan histori konfigurasi.","Benar — Config timeline menampilkan konfigurasi bucket pada waktu tertentu dan semua perubahan sesudahnya.","Salah — Access logs mencatat request ke objek/bucket, bukan snapshot konfigurasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'configuration at a point in time / configuration history' → AWS Config; 'who made the API call' → CloudTrail."},{"id":"E4A-49","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation with Redshift Spectrum","q":"An Amazon Redshift cluster queries data lake tables through an external schema that was created with CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA ... FROM DATA CATALOG ... IAM_ROLE 'arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/RedshiftSpectrumRole'. After the company turned on AWS Lake Formation permissions for the Data Catalog, Redshift Spectrum queries on the external tables fail with access denied errors. What should a data engineer do to restore access while keeping Lake Formation as the authorization layer?","o":["Attach the AmazonS3FullAccess managed policy to RedshiftSpectrumRole.","In Lake Formation, grant DESCRIBE on the database and SELECT on the required tables (or columns) to RedshiftSpectrumRole.","Re-create the external schema with the Redshift service-linked role instead of RedshiftSpectrumRole.","Grant SELECT on the external tables to the Redshift users with a GRANT statement in Redshift."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'after the company turned on AWS Lake Formation permissions' dan 'keeping Lake Formation as the authorization layer'. Saat Redshift Spectrum membaca tabel Data Catalog yang diatur Lake Formation, principal yang dievaluasi oleh Lake Formation adalah IAM role yang dipakai di external schema. Karena itu role tersebut harus diberi izin Lake Formation, yaitu DESCRIBE pada database dan SELECT pada tabel atau kolom yang dibutuhkan, dan Lake Formation akan memberikan credential sementara ke lokasi data. Menambah izin S3 di IAM melewati model Lake Formation dan tidak menyelesaikan penolakan dari Lake Formation. Service-linked role tidak dipakai untuk external schema. GRANT di Redshift hanya mengatur user Redshift mana yang boleh memakai schema, tetapi akses ke data lake tetap ditolak jika role belum mendapat izin Lake Formation. Aturan umum: Redshift Spectrum + Lake Formation → grant Lake Formation ke IAM role external schema.","r":["Salah — Izin S3 lebar tidak menyelesaikan penolakan dari Lake Formation dan melanggar least privilege.","Benar — Lake Formation mengevaluasi IAM role external schema, sehingga role itu perlu izin DESCRIBE dan SELECT.","Salah — Service-linked role Redshift tidak dirancang untuk akses data Spectrum dan tidak bisa diatur seperti ini.","Salah — GRANT Redshift saja tidak cukup jika Lake Formation menolak akses role ke tabel."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift Spectrum ditolak setelah Lake Formation aktif → grant Lake Formation ke IAM role di CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA."},{"id":"E2B-59","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"Redshift Multi-AZ","q":"A business-critical Amazon Redshift RA3 provisioned cluster serves dashboards that must stay available if one Availability Zone fails. The business requires the LOWEST recovery time without changing the application's connection endpoint and without manual intervention. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Rely on cluster relocation so that Redshift moves the cluster to another AZ during an outage.","Restore the latest automated snapshot into a new cluster in another AZ when an outage occurs.","Configure cross-Region snapshot copy to another Region.","Deploy the cluster as a Redshift Multi-AZ deployment so that compute runs in two AZs and fails over automatically."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'one Availability Zone fails', 'LOWEST recovery time', 'without changing the application's connection endpoint' dan 'without manual intervention'. Redshift Multi-AZ (untuk cluster provisioned RA3/RG) menjalankan compute di dua AZ dengan satu endpoint; jika satu AZ gagal, workload otomatis dilayani dari AZ lain tanpa perubahan pada aplikasi. Cluster relocation juga mempertahankan endpoint dan bisa memindahkan cluster saat ada masalah kapasitas AZ, tetapi terjadi outage selama cluster baru dinyalakan di AZ lain dan relokasi tidak selalu mungkin jika kapasitas AZ terbatas, sehingga RTO lebih tinggi daripada Multi-AZ (Multi-AZ menaikkan SLA ke 99,99%). Restore snapshot manual menghasilkan endpoint baru dan RTO yang lama. Cross-Region snapshot copy untuk bencana tingkat Region dan butuh restore. Ingat: Redshift HA terhadap kegagalan AZ dengan RTO terendah → Multi-AZ; DR Region → cross-Region snapshot.","r":["Salah — Relocation mempertahankan endpoint, tetapi waktu pemulihannya lebih lama dibandingkan Multi-AZ.","Salah — Restore snapshot manual butuh intervensi, menghasilkan endpoint baru, dan RTO panjang.","Salah — Cross-Region snapshot ditujukan untuk bencana Region dan tetap membutuhkan restore manual.","Benar — Multi-AZ memberi failover otomatis antar-AZ dengan endpoint yang sama dan RTO terendah."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift + 'AZ failure' + 'lowest RTO, automatic' → Redshift Multi-AZ (RA3)."},{"id":"E3B-49","d":3,"ts":"3.4.2","t":"DQDL ReferentialIntegrity","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job processes an orders dataset and has access to a customers dataset as an additional data source with the alias 'reference'. Every customer_id in the orders must exist in the customers dataset; otherwise the job must fail. Which DQDL rule meets this requirement?","o":["IsComplete \"customer_id\"","ReferentialIntegrity \"customer_id\" \"reference.customer_id\" = 1.0","IsUnique \"customer_id\"","ColumnValues \"customer_id\" > 0"],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'every customer_id in the orders must exist in the customers dataset' — ini adalah pemeriksaan integritas referensial antar dataset. Rule ReferentialIntegrity di DQDL membandingkan kolom pada dataset utama dengan kolom pada dataset referensi (alias 'reference') dan menghasilkan rasio nilai yang ditemukan; = 1.0 berarti 100% harus cocok. Distraktor terdekat adalah IsComplete: hanya memastikan customer_id terisi, tetapi nilai yang terisi bisa saja tidak ada di tabel customers (orphan). IsUnique justru salah karena satu customer dapat memiliki banyak order. ColumnValues > 0 hanya memeriksa rentang nilai. Aturan: foreign key / orphan records antar dataset → ReferentialIntegrity.","r":["Salah — Hanya memeriksa nilai tidak kosong, bukan keberadaannya di tabel customers.","Benar — ReferentialIntegrity memastikan 100% customer_id ditemukan di dataset referensi.","Salah — customer_id boleh berulang di orders, dan keunikan tidak menjamin keberadaan di tabel referensi.","Salah — Rentang nilai tidak membuktikan bahwa customer tersebut ada."],"k":"Tips ujian: orphan keys / 'must exist in another dataset' → DQDL ReferentialIntegrity."},{"id":"E1B-01","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"AWS Glue vs EMR vs Lambda for batch ETL","q":"A retail company receives about 50 GB of CSV sales files in an Amazon S3 bucket every night. A data engineer must clean the data, apply business rules, and write the results as Apache Parquet to another S3 prefix before 6 AM. The team already writes PySpark code and does not want to provision or manage any clusters. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Launch an Amazon EMR cluster on Amazon EC2 every night with a bootstrap action that runs the PySpark script, and terminate the cluster after the step completes.","Create an AWS Glue Spark ETL job that runs the PySpark script on a nightly schedule and writes Parquet output to Amazon S3.","Use an AWS Lambda function triggered by an S3 event to load each CSV file into memory, transform it with pandas, and write Parquet output.","Run the PySpark script with a cron job on a large Amazon EC2 instance that has Apache Spark installed."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'does not want to provision or manage any clusters' dan 'LEAST operational overhead', ditambah volume 50 GB per malam dan tim yang sudah menguasai PySpark. AWS Glue ETL job adalah layanan Spark serverless: kode PySpark bisa dijalankan apa adanya, kapasitas (DPU/worker) dikelola AWS, dan penjadwalan bisa memakai Glue trigger. Opsi EMR on EC2 juga bisa menjalankan Spark, tetapi Anda tetap harus mengelola konfigurasi cluster, bootstrap action, dan siklus hidup cluster. Lambda dibatasi timeout 15 menit dan memori maksimum 10 GB sehingga tidak cocok untuk transformasi 50 GB dengan Spark. EC2 dengan cron adalah opsi dengan overhead paling tinggi karena Anda mengelola OS, instalasi Spark, dan skalabilitas sendiri. Aturan umum: transformasi batch berbasis Spark tanpa ingin mengelola server → AWS Glue ETL job.","r":["Salah — EMR on EC2 bisa menjalankan PySpark, tetapi tetap ada pengelolaan cluster (instance type, bootstrap, terminasi), sehingga overhead lebih besar daripada Glue.","Benar — Glue ETL job adalah Spark serverless yang menjalankan kode PySpark yang ada, dijadwalkan dengan trigger, dan menulis Parquet ke S3 tanpa mengelola cluster.","Salah — Lambda punya batas waktu 15 menit dan memori terbatas; memproses 50 GB dengan pandas di Lambda tidak andal dan bukan Spark.","Salah — EC2 dengan cron menuntut pengelolaan OS, instalasi Spark, dan kapasitas secara manual; overhead operasional tertinggi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Spark/PySpark + serverless + least operational overhead' → AWS Glue ETL job."},{"id":"E3A-01","d":3,"ts":"3.1.1","t":"Step Functions vs MWAA orchestration","q":"A data engineering team runs a nightly pipeline: an AWS Glue ETL job transforms raw CSV files in Amazon S3, then an Amazon Athena query builds a summary table, and an Amazon SNS alert must be sent if any step fails. The team has no Apache Airflow experience and wants a visual, serverless orchestrator. Each step must start only after the previous step has fully completed. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an Amazon MWAA environment and write an Airflow DAG that uses the Glue and Athena operators, with an on_failure_callback that publishes to SNS.","Create an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow that uses the Glue StartJobRun and Athena StartQueryExecution service integrations with the .sync pattern, and add a Catch that routes failures to an SNS Publish state.","Create an AWS Lambda function that starts the Glue job, polls it until completion, then starts the Athena query and polls it, and publishes to SNS on error.","Schedule a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance that runs AWS CLI commands for Glue and Athena in sequence and calls SNS on a non-zero exit code."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'visual, serverless orchestrator', tim 'no Apache Airflow experience', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Step Functions Standard workflow adalah orkestrator serverless dengan editor visual (Workflow Studio) dan punya service integration langsung ke Glue dan Athena. Pola integrasi '.sync' (Run a Job) membuat state menunggu sampai Glue job atau query Athena benar-benar selesai, tanpa kode polling. Blok Catch mengarahkan error apa pun ke state SNS Publish, sehingga notifikasi kegagalan juga tanpa kode. Amazon MWAA memang bisa, tetapi butuh skill Airflow, menulis DAG Python, dan environment yang berjalan terus (biaya dan overhead lebih tinggi). Lambda yang mem-polling Glue job berisiko terkena batas timeout 15 menit dan menambah kode yang harus dirawat. Aturan umum: untuk orkestrasi layanan AWS yang serverless dan visual tanpa skill Airflow, pilih Step Functions dengan integrasi .sync.","r":["Salah — MWAA berfungsi, tetapi tim tidak punya skill Airflow dan environment MWAA berjalan terus-menerus sehingga overhead dan biayanya lebih besar.","Benar — Step Functions serverless dan visual; .sync menunggu Glue/Athena selesai dan Catch ke SNS menangani kegagalan tanpa kode tambahan.","Salah — Polling di dalam Lambda menambah kode dan bisa melewati batas timeout 15 menit jika Glue job berjalan lama.","Salah — EC2 cron bukan serverless; Anda harus mengelola instance, patching, dan penanganan error sendiri."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'serverless + visual + tunggu job selesai' → Step Functions dengan integrasi .sync; 'sudah punya DAG Airflow' → MWAA."},{"id":"E1C-26","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions Standard workflow semantics","q":"A financial reconciliation pipeline runs for about 2 hours and calls several non-idempotent payment APIs. Auditors require that each step runs exactly once and that the full step-by-step execution history can be retrieved for up to 90 days without additional configuration. Which AWS Step Functions configuration meets these requirements?","o":["An asynchronous Express workflow with logging to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","A synchronous Express workflow started from Amazon API Gateway.","A Standard workflow.","An Express workflow that is restarted every 5 minutes with the previous output as input."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhan pembeda: durasi 'about 2 hours', API 'non-idempotent' yang harus jalan 'exactly once', dan riwayat eksekusi '90 days without additional configuration'. Standard workflow dapat berjalan hingga 1 tahun, memiliki semantik exactly-once untuk eksekusi workflow, dan menyimpan riwayat eksekusi selama 90 hari yang bisa dilihat di konsol atau API. Distractor terdekat adalah Express dengan CloudWatch Logs: riwayat hanya tersedia jika logging dikonfigurasi (konfigurasi tambahan), durasinya maksimum 5 menit, dan semantik asinkronnya at-least-once yang berbahaya untuk API non-idempotent. Express sinkron bersifat at-most-once dan tetap terbatas 5 menit. Merangkai Express setiap 5 menit sangat rapuh. Aturan umum: long-running, audit, exactly-once → Standard workflow.","r":["Salah — Express asinkron bersifat at-least-once, maksimum 5 menit, dan riwayat butuh konfigurasi logging.","Salah — Express sinkron juga dibatasi 5 menit.","Benar — Standard mendukung durasi panjang, exactly-once, dan riwayat 90 hari secara bawaan.","Salah — Merangkai eksekusi pendek rapuh dan tetap tidak memberi jaminan exactly-once."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'exactly-once' + 'long-running' + 'execution history/audit' → Standard workflow."},{"id":"E3B-01","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"CloudTrail Event history","q":"A security auditor asks a data engineer to identify which IAM principal deleted an AWS Glue Data Catalog table 12 days ago. The company has never created a CloudTrail trail or configured AWS Config. Which solution will provide the answer with the LEAST effort?","o":["Create a CloudTrail trail now and query the delivered log files in Amazon S3 with Amazon Athena.","Search the CloudTrail Event history in the console for the DeleteTable event name in the last 90 days.","Run a CloudWatch Logs Insights query against the Glue job log groups for the word 'DeleteTable'.","Enable AWS Config recording for Glue resources and review the configuration timeline of the table."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan jawaban adalah 'never created a CloudTrail trail' dan kejadian '12 days ago'. CloudTrail Event history aktif secara default di setiap akun dan menyimpan management events selama 90 hari tanpa perlu membuat trail. DeleteTable pada Glue Data Catalog adalah management event, sehingga muncul di Event history lengkap dengan userIdentity, waktu, dan source IP. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat trail baru lalu query dengan Athena, tetapi trail hanya merekam event SETELAH dibuat sehingga kejadian 12 hari lalu tidak akan ada. AWS Config juga baru merekam setelah diaktifkan dan bukan alat utama untuk 'siapa memanggil API'. Aturan umum: pertanyaan 'siapa melakukan apa' dalam 90 hari terakhir tanpa setup apa pun → CloudTrail Event history.","r":["Salah — Trail hanya mencatat event sejak trail dibuat, jadi penghapusan 12 hari lalu tidak akan ada di S3.","Benar — Event history menyimpan management events 90 hari secara default dan bisa difilter berdasarkan event name DeleteTable untuk melihat principal pelakunya.","Salah — Log group Glue job berisi output aplikasi Spark, bukan catatan panggilan API Data Catalog oleh principal.","Salah — AWS Config tidak merekam ke belakang dan fokus pada perubahan konfigurasi resource, bukan identitas pemanggil API."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'who did it' + kurang dari 90 hari + belum ada trail → CloudTrail Event history."},{"id":"E3A-30","d":3,"ts":"3.1.8","t":"Lambda Kinesis error handling","q":"An AWS Lambda function consumes records from an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream through an event source mapping. Occasionally a malformed record causes the function to throw an error, and the whole shard stops progressing because the same batch is retried repeatedly until the records expire. The data engineer wants healthy records to keep flowing and wants to keep failed records for later analysis. Which TWO configuration changes should the data engineer make? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Increase the batch size of the event source mapping to 10,000 records.","Increase the function's memory and timeout.","Enable BisectBatchOnFunctionError on the event source mapping.","Set MaximumRetryAttempts (or a maximum record age) and configure an on-failure destination such as an Amazon SQS queue.","Increase the parallelization factor of the event source mapping."],"a":[2,3],"e":"Gejalanya adalah 'poison record' yang membuat shard macet karena batch yang sama diulang terus. Opsi BisectBatchOnFunctionError membelah batch yang gagal menjadi dua dan mengulang masing-masing, sehingga record yang rusak terisolasi dan record sehat tetap diproses. MaximumRetryAttempts atau maximum record age membatasi berapa lama record gagal diulang, dan on-failure destination (SQS atau SNS) menyimpan informasi record yang gagal untuk dianalisis, sesuai syarat 'keep failed records'. Menambah batch size memperburuk masalah karena lebih banyak record ikut gagal. Memori dan timeout tidak memperbaiki record yang formatnya salah. Parallelization factor menambah concurrency per shard, tetapi batch yang gagal tetap memblokir urutan untuk partition key yang sama. Aturan umum: Lambda + Kinesis/DynamoDB Streams dengan poison record → bisect batch + batas retry + on-failure destination.","r":["Salah — Batch yang lebih besar membuat lebih banyak record ikut gagal bersama record rusak.","Salah — Error berasal dari data yang rusak, bukan dari kekurangan memori atau waktu.","Benar — Membelah batch mengisolasi record rusak sehingga record sehat tetap diproses.","Benar — Batas retry menghentikan pengulangan tanpa akhir dan destination menyimpan record yang gagal.","Salah — Concurrency per shard bertambah, tetapi batch yang gagal tetap diulang tanpa akhir."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda stream 'poison record blocks shard' → BisectBatchOnFunctionError + MaximumRetryAttempts + on-failure destination."},{"id":"E1B-58","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"API Gateway usage plans","q":"A company provides a data API built with Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda to several external partners. Each partner must be identified separately and must have its own maximum request rate and monthly request quota based on its contract. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create a separate API Gateway API and Lambda function for each partner.","Create API keys for each partner and associate them with API Gateway usage plans that define throttling limits and quotas.","Configure AWS WAF rate-based rules for each partner's IP address range.","Implement request counting in the Lambda function with a DynamoDB table per partner."],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah kebutuhan per partner: 'identified separately', 'maximum request rate', dan 'monthly request quota', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. API Gateway usage plans memungkinkan Anda membuat API key per partner dan menetapkan throttling (rate dan burst) serta quota (per hari, minggu, atau bulan) tanpa kode tambahan. Membuat API terpisah per partner menggandakan infrastruktur dan pemeliharaan. AWS WAF rate-based rules membatasi laju per IP, tetapi tidak menyediakan kuota bulanan per kontrak dan IP partner bisa berubah. Penghitungan request di Lambda dengan DynamoDB adalah kode kustom yang harus dipelihara. Catatan: API key berfungsi untuk identifikasi dan metering, bukan mekanisme autentikasi/otorisasi; untuk kontrol akses tetap gunakan IAM, Amazon Cognito, atau Lambda authorizer. Aturan umum: throttling dan kuota per konsumen API → API Gateway usage plans + API keys.","r":["Salah — Menggandakan API dan fungsi untuk setiap partner menambah overhead besar.","Benar — Usage plans dengan API keys memberi rate limit dan kuota per partner secara bawaan.","Salah — WAF membatasi laju per IP, tidak menyediakan kuota bulanan per partner.","Salah — Logika penghitungan kustom menambah kode, biaya, dan pemeliharaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'per-client throttling and quotas on API' → API Gateway usage plans + API keys."},{"id":"E3B-38","d":3,"ts":"3.3.6","t":"Athena partition projection for pipeline maintenance","q":"An S3 data lake table is partitioned by year, month, day, and hour, and new partitions arrive every hour. Amazon Athena queries frequently miss the latest data because the AWS Glue crawler that adds partitions runs only once a day, and running MSCK REPAIR TABLE takes a long time. Which solution reduces this maintenance burden the MOST?","o":["Schedule the crawler to run every 5 minutes.","Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE from an AWS Lambda function after every file upload.","Configure partition projection on the table so that Athena calculates partition values from the table properties instead of the Data Catalog.","Remove partitioning from the table so that no partitions need to be registered."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'queries miss the latest data', 'new partitions every hour', dan 'reduces this maintenance burden the MOST'. Partition projection membuat Athena menghitung partisi dari properti tabel (rentang dan format nilai) saat query, sehingga partisi baru langsung dapat di-query tanpa crawler, ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION, atau MSCK REPAIR. Untuk tabel dengan pola partisi berbasis waktu yang sangat banyak, ini juga mempercepat perencanaan query. Distraktor terdekat adalah crawler setiap 5 menit: menambah biaya, tetap ada jeda, dan masih harus dipantau. Lambda yang menjalankan MSCK REPAIR setiap upload lambat dan mahal. Menghapus partisi membuat setiap query memindai seluruh data. Aturan: partisi time-based yang terus bertambah → Athena partition projection.","r":["Salah — Crawler yang sering berjalan menambah biaya dan tetap menyisakan jeda serta pekerjaan pemantauan.","Salah — MSCK REPAIR lambat dan menjalankannya per file sangat tidak efisien.","Benar — Partition projection menghilangkan kebutuhan mendaftarkan partisi sehingga data terbaru langsung terbaca.","Salah — Tanpa partisi, setiap query memindai seluruh data dan biayanya naik drastis."],"k":"Tips ujian: partisi baru tidak terlihat di Athena + ingin tanpa maintenance → partition projection."},{"id":"E2C-12","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Glue Schema Registry compatibility","q":"Several producer applications write Avro records to Amazon MSK topics, and dozens of consumer applications read them. Producers occasionally change the record schema, and last month a producer removed a required field, which broke several consumers. The company wants to prevent incompatible schema changes from being published while allowing safe evolution. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store the Avro schema as a JSON file in Amazon S3 and ask each team to review it manually before deploying producers.","Use the AWS Glue Schema Registry with the producers' and consumers' serializers, and set an appropriate compatibility mode such as BACKWARD on the schema.","Convert all records to CSV so that consumers ignore unknown columns.","Create a new MSK topic for each schema version and have consumers subscribe to all topics."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'prevent incompatible schema changes from being published while allowing safe evolution' pada data streaming Avro. AWS Glue Schema Registry terintegrasi dengan Amazon MSK, Kinesis Data Streams, dan Managed Service for Apache Flink melalui library serializer/deserializer. Setiap versi schema baru diperiksa terhadap compatibility mode (misalnya BACKWARD, FORWARD, FULL); jika tidak kompatibel, registrasi versi ditolak sehingga producer tidak dapat mengirim data dengan schema yang merusak consumer. Review manual file di S3 tidak memberikan penegakan otomatis dan rawan kesalahan manusia. CSV justru menghilangkan tipe data dan validasi schema. Topik baru per versi schema menambah kompleksitas operasional di semua consumer. Aturan umum: penegakan evolusi schema untuk streaming di AWS → Glue Schema Registry dengan compatibility mode.","r":["Salah — Review manual tidak menegakkan kompatibilitas secara otomatis dan mudah terlewat.","Benar — Glue Schema Registry memvalidasi setiap versi schema terhadap compatibility mode dan menolak perubahan yang tidak kompatibel.","Salah — CSV menghilangkan tipe data dan tidak memberikan kontrak schema apa pun.","Salah — Topik per versi schema memperumit consumer dan tidak mencegah perubahan yang merusak."],"k":"Tips ujian: Kafka/Kinesis + cegah perubahan schema yang merusak → AWS Glue Schema Registry + compatibility mode."},{"id":"E4A-26","d":4,"ts":"4.1.7","t":"SageMaker Unified Studio projects and membership","q":"In Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio, a team of six data engineers needs a shared space for their notebooks, SQL queries, and workflows, with a shared Git repository and access to the data assets the team subscribes to. Two contractors must have the same access only while their engagement lasts. Which approach meets these requirements?","o":["Create a separate domain for the team and add the contractors as domain administrators.","Create a project from an approved project profile, add the engineers and contractors as project members, and remove the contractors when the engagement ends.","Share the project's IAM role credentials with the contractors through AWS Secrets Manager.","Publish all of the team's notebooks to the business catalog so that the contractors can find them."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'shared space', 'shared Git repository', 'access to subscribed data', dan akses kontraktor 'only while their engagement lasts'. Di SageMaker Unified Studio, project adalah wadah kerja tim: batas kolaborasi (repository Git bersama) dan batas permission (anggota mendapat akses ke artefak project serta izin data dan compute). Project dibuat dari project profile yang menentukan tool yang tersedia. Owner project dapat menambah anggota sebagai owner atau contributor dan menghapusnya kapan saja, sehingga akses kontraktor mudah dicabut. Domain terpisah dan peran domain administrator memberi hak jauh melebihi kebutuhan. Berbagi credential role melanggar praktik keamanan dan tidak dapat diaudit per orang. Publikasi ke business catalog ditujukan untuk asset data, bukan berbagi ruang kerja. Aturan umum: kolaborasi tim + batas akses di SageMaker Unified Studio → project dan project membership.","r":["Salah — Domain administrator memiliki hak terlalu besar, dan domain baru menambah overhead.","Benar — Project memberi ruang kerja bersama, repository Git, dan akses data, sementara membership bisa ditambah atau dicabut sesuai kebutuhan.","Salah — Berbagi credential role tidak aman dan tidak bisa diaudit per pengguna.","Salah — Business catalog untuk menemukan asset data, bukan untuk memberi akses ruang kerja project."],"k":"Tips ujian: project = batas kolaborasi dan batas permission; tambah/hapus member (owner/contributor) untuk mengatur akses."},{"id":"E4B-36","d":4,"ts":"4.5.7","t":"Data mesh governance pattern","q":"A large enterprise has 12 business units. Each unit wants to own, build, and publish its own datasets as data products in its own AWS account, while a central team defines common governance rules and provides a single place where other units can discover and request access to the data products. Data should not be copied into a central account. Which data architecture pattern BEST meets these requirements?","o":["A centralized data lake in which every business unit copies its data into one central S3 bucket managed by the central team.","A data mesh in which producer accounts keep their data and publish it to a central governed catalog (for example, Amazon SageMaker Catalog or AWS Lake Formation in a central governance account) that grants consumers access through cross-account sharing.","Ad hoc sharing in which each business unit writes S3 bucket policies for every consumer account that asks for data.","Nightly exports of each unit's data to CSV files that are sent to consumers over SFTP with AWS Transfer Family."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: tiap unit ingin 'own, build, and publish its own datasets as data products in its own AWS account', ada 'common governance rules' terpusat, satu tempat untuk 'discover and request access', dan 'should not be copied into a central account'. Ini adalah definisi data mesh: kepemilikan data terdesentralisasi per domain, sementara governance dan katalog bersifat federatif/terpusat. Di AWS, producer mempublikasikan data ke katalog terkelola (SageMaker Catalog atau Lake Formation di governance account) dan consumer mendapat akses melalui sharing lintas akun tanpa menyalin data. Distraktor terdekat adalah data lake terpusat: governance-nya mudah, tetapi menyalin data ke akun pusat dan memindahkan kepemilikan ke tim pusat, melanggar dua syarat. Bucket policy ad hoc tidak memiliki katalog terpusat maupun governance konsisten. Ekspor CSV via SFTP menyalin data dan menghasilkan data basi. Aturan umum: 'domain ownership + central governance + no copies' → data mesh.","r":["Salah — Data disalin ke akun pusat dan kepemilikan berpindah ke tim pusat, bertentangan dengan syarat.","Benar — Data mesh menjaga kepemilikan di producer, dengan katalog dan governance terpusat serta sharing lintas akun tanpa salinan.","Salah — Bucket policy ad hoc tidak memberi katalog penemuan terpusat atau aturan governance yang konsisten.","Salah — Ekspor CSV menyalin data, membuat data basi, dan tidak menyediakan governance terpusat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'domains own data products + central catalog/governance + no copy' → data mesh (Lake Formation/SageMaker Catalog)."},{"id":"E1C-61","d":1,"ts":"1.4.7","t":"Mounting Amazon EFS in Lambda","q":"Several AWS Lambda functions in a data pipeline need low-latency read and write access to the same 5 GB set of reference files by using standard file system operations. An application on Amazon EC2 already updates these files on an existing Amazon EFS file system, and the Lambda functions must always see the latest version. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Package the reference files in a Lambda layer and attach the layer to each function.","Copy the files into each function's /tmp ephemeral storage at the start of every invocation.","Configure each Lambda function to connect to the VPC and mount the existing EFS file system through an EFS access point.","Store the files in the function deployment package and redeploy the functions whenever the EC2 application changes a file."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: beberapa fungsi berbagi 'read and write access' ke file 5 GB yang 'already updates ... on an existing Amazon EFS', dan harus selalu melihat versi terbaru. Lambda dapat me-mount Amazon EFS melalui access point (fungsi harus terhubung ke VPC yang memiliki mount target), sehingga semua fungsi dan aplikasi EC2 berbagi file system POSIX yang sama secara langsung dan konsisten. Distractor terdekat adalah salin ke /tmp setiap invocation: data tidak dibagikan, tulisan tidak terlihat oleh fungsi lain, dan menyalin 5 GB berulang kali lambat. Lambda layer dan deployment package bersifat statis, dibatasi 250 MB (unzipped), dan memerlukan redeploy untuk setiap perubahan. Aturan umum: storage bersama, persisten, dan bisa ditulis untuk Lambda → mount EFS. Catatan pembaruan: sejak April 2026 Lambda juga dapat me-mount bucket S3 sebagai file system melalui Amazon S3 Files (dibangun di atas EFS); fitur ini belum tercantum di exam guide DEA-C01.","r":["Salah — Layer bersifat read-only, statis, dan dibatasi 250 MB unzipped.","Salah — /tmp tidak dibagikan antar fungsi dan menyalin 5 GB per invocation lambat.","Benar — Mount EFS via access point memberi akses baca/tulis bersama yang selalu terbaru.","Salah — Paket deployment terbatas ukurannya dan perlu redeploy untuk setiap perubahan."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda butuh file system bersama/persisten → Amazon EFS (fungsi dalam VPC, access point)."},{"id":"E2C-01","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Redshift distribution styles for star schema","q":"A retail company is building a star schema in Amazon Redshift. The SALES fact table has 4 billion rows and is almost always joined to the CUSTOMER dimension (60 million rows) on customer_id. Small dimension tables such as STORE (2,000 rows) and PROMOTION (500 rows) are also joined in most queries. The company wants to minimize data redistribution during joins. Which TWO table designs should the data engineer use? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use DISTSTYLE KEY with customer_id as the distribution key on both SALES and CUSTOMER.","Use DISTSTYLE ALL on SALES so that every node has a full copy of the fact table.","Use DISTSTYLE ALL on the small STORE and PROMOTION dimension tables.","Use DISTSTYLE EVEN on CUSTOMER and DISTSTYLE KEY on SALES with store_id as the distribution key.","Use an interleaved sort key on customer_id for all tables instead of choosing a distribution style."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'minimize data redistribution during joins' pada star schema dengan fact table sangat besar. Di Amazon Redshift, join antara dua tabel besar paling efisien jika keduanya didistribusikan dengan DISTSTYLE KEY pada kolom join yang sama (customer_id), sehingga baris yang cocok berada di slice yang sama (collocated join). Untuk dimension table kecil seperti STORE dan PROMOTION, DISTSTYLE ALL menaruh salinan penuh di setiap node sehingga join dengan fact table tidak perlu broadcast atau redistribusi. DISTSTYLE ALL untuk fact table 4 miliar baris justru memboroskan storage dan memperlambat load. DISTSTYLE EVEN pada CUSTOMER memaksa redistribusi karena baris tidak lagi collocated dengan SALES. Sort key tidak menggantikan distribution style; sort key membantu filtering (zone maps), bukan collocation join. Aturan umum: KEY untuk pasangan tabel besar yang sering di-join, ALL untuk dimensi kecil yang jarang berubah.","r":["Benar — KEY pada customer_id di kedua tabel membuat join SALES–CUSTOMER collocated di slice yang sama tanpa redistribusi.","Salah — Menyalin fact table 4 miliar baris ke setiap node memboroskan storage dan memperlambat load; ALL hanya cocok untuk tabel kecil.","Benar — Dimensi kecil dengan DISTSTYLE ALL tersedia lengkap di setiap node sehingga join tidak memerlukan broadcast.","Salah — EVEN pada CUSTOMER dan KEY store_id pada SALES membuat join utama pada customer_id tidak collocated sehingga terjadi redistribusi.","Salah — Sort key membantu pruning blok saat filter, bukan menghindari redistribusi saat join; interleaved sort key juga menambah overhead VACUUM."],"k":"Tips ujian: join dua tabel besar → DISTSTYLE KEY pada kolom join; dimensi kecil → DISTSTYLE ALL."},{"id":"E1C-01","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Step Functions .sync service integrations","q":"A data engineering team runs a nightly pipeline that starts an AWS Glue ETL job, then runs an Amazon Athena CTAS query on the job output, and finally invokes an AWS Lambda function that updates a status table. Each step must start only after the previous step has fully completed, and failures must be visible in a single visual execution history. The team has no Apache Airflow experience. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an AWS Step Functions state machine that uses the optimized Glue StartJobRun.sync and Athena StartQueryExecution.sync integrations, followed by a Lambda Invoke task, and schedule it with Amazon EventBridge Scheduler.","Write one Lambda function that starts the Glue job, polls GetJobRun in a loop until it finishes, then starts the Athena query and polls until it completes.","Deploy an Amazon MWAA environment and write a DAG that uses the Glue, Athena, and Lambda operators from the Amazon provider package.","Run a cron script on an Amazon EC2 instance that calls the AWS CLI for each step and writes progress to a log file on the instance."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan jawaban adalah 'fully completed', 'single visual execution history', dan 'LEAST operational overhead' dengan tim yang belum paham Airflow. AWS Step Functions punya integrasi teroptimasi dengan pola '.sync' (Run a Job) untuk Glue dan Athena, sehingga state machine otomatis menunggu job selesai tanpa kode polling. Riwayat eksekusi visual per step tersedia langsung di konsol Step Functions, dan EventBridge Scheduler menjalankan state machine setiap malam tanpa server. Distractor terdekat adalah MWAA: secara teknis bisa, tetapi tim harus belajar Airflow dan mengelola environment yang berjalan terus (biaya dan overhead lebih tinggi). Opsi Lambda polling berisiko melewati batas timeout 15 menit dan menyatukan semua logika dalam satu fungsi tanpa visibilitas per step. Aturan umum: untuk orkestrasi serverless antar layanan AWS dengan dependensi berurutan, pilih Step Functions dengan integrasi '.sync'.","r":["Benar — Integrasi '.sync' menunggu Glue job dan query Athena selesai, riwayat eksekusi visual tersedia, dan semuanya serverless dengan jadwal dari EventBridge Scheduler.","Salah — Polling dalam Lambda dibatasi timeout 15 menit, membuang biaya komputasi selama menunggu, dan tidak memberi riwayat visual per step.","Salah — MWAA bisa mengorkestrasi, tetapi menambah overhead (environment selalu aktif, kurva belajar Airflow) yang tidak sesuai syarat LEAST operational overhead.","Salah — Cron di EC2 adalah single point of failure, harus dipatch dan dikelola, serta tidak memberi visibilitas kegagalan yang terpusat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'tunggu job selesai' + 'serverless' + 'visual workflow' → Step Functions dengan integrasi .sync."},{"id":"E2A-01","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Kinesis Data Streams vs Data Firehose vs SQS","q":"A retail company collects clickstream events from its website at about 20 MB/s. Three independent applications must consume the same events in real time with millisecond latency: a fraud detector, a recommendation engine, and an archiver. The fraud team must be able to replay the last 5 days of events after a model fix. Which storage solution meets these requirements?","o":["Send the events to Amazon Data Firehose and deliver them to Amazon S3 every 60 seconds.","Send the events to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams with the retention period extended to 7 days, and attach each application as a separate consumer.","Send the events to an Amazon SQS standard queue that all three applications poll.","Write the events directly to an Amazon S3 bucket and use S3 Event Notifications to trigger each application."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'three independent applications', 'real time with millisecond latency', dan 'replay the last 5 days'. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams menyimpan record secara terurut per shard, mendukung banyak consumer yang membaca stream yang sama secara independen, dan retention bisa diperpanjang dari default 24 jam hingga 365 hari. Dengan retention 7 hari, tim fraud bisa membaca ulang (replay) dari posisi atau timestamp tertentu. Distraktor terdekat adalah Data Firehose, tetapi Firehose adalah layanan delivery near-real-time yang mengirim data ke destinasi (dengan buffering, umumnya hitungan detik hingga menit) dan tidak menyediakan replay atau banyak consumer yang membaca stream yang sama. SQS menghapus pesan setelah diproses sehingga tiga consumer akan saling berebut pesan. Aturan umum: butuh multi-consumer + replay + latensi rendah = Kinesis Data Streams (atau MSK), bukan Firehose atau SQS.","r":["Salah — Firehose mem-buffer lalu mengirim ke S3 (di sini setiap 60 detik), sehingga latensinya bukan milidetik dan tidak ada kemampuan replay atau multi-consumer real time.","Benar — Kinesis Data Streams mendukung banyak consumer independen, latensi rendah, dan retention yang bisa diperpanjang untuk replay data 5 hari.","Salah — Pesan SQS dihapus setelah diproses oleh satu consumer, jadi tiga aplikasi tidak bisa membaca event yang sama dan replay tidak mungkin.","Salah — Menulis setiap event kecil sebagai object S3 mahal dan tidak memberi pemrosesan stream terurut; replay harus dibangun sendiri."],"k":"Multiple consumers + replay + real time → Kinesis Data Streams dengan retention diperpanjang; Firehose = delivery near-real-time tanpa replay."},{"id":"E3B-13","d":3,"ts":"3.3.2","t":"AWS Glue continuous logging","q":"A data engineer maintains an AWS Glue 4.0 Spark ETL job that runs for about 2 hours. The script writes custom progress messages with a logger. Operators want to watch the driver and executor log output, including the custom messages, while the job is still running instead of waiting for the run to finish. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Enable job bookmarks on the job.","Enable the Spark UI and store Spark event logs in Amazon S3.","Enable AWS Glue continuous logging for the job so that logs stream to CloudWatch Logs during the run.","Create a CloudTrail trail with data events for AWS Glue."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'while the job is still running' dan 'custom messages'. AWS Glue continuous logging (parameter --enable-continuous-cloudwatch-log) mengalirkan log driver dan executor ke CloudWatch Logs secara real time selama job berjalan, termasuk pesan dari logger aplikasi, dan bisa disertai filter untuk mengurangi noise Spark. Distraktor terdekat adalah Spark UI event logs di S3: berguna untuk menganalisis stage, task, dan eksekusi, tetapi tidak menampilkan pesan log kustom dari script. Job bookmarks mengatur pemrosesan inkremental, tidak terkait logging. CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan output aplikasi. Aturan: lihat log Glue secara real time → continuous logging ke CloudWatch Logs.","r":["Salah — Job bookmarks melacak data yang sudah diproses, bukan menampilkan log.","Salah — Spark UI membantu analisis performa stage/task, tetapi tidak menampilkan pesan log kustom dari script.","Benar — Continuous logging mengalirkan log driver/executor beserta pesan kustom ke CloudWatch Logs selama job berjalan.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API Glue, bukan log aplikasi job."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'real-time Glue job logs' → continuous logging ke CloudWatch Logs."},{"id":"E2A-13","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"DynamoDB GSI vs LSI","q":"An Amazon DynamoDB table named Orders uses customer_id as the partition key and order_timestamp as the sort key. The table is already in production with 2 TB of data. A new feature must retrieve all orders that contain a specific product_id, and eventually consistent reads are acceptable. Which solution meets this requirement MOST efficiently?","o":["Create a global secondary index (GSI) with product_id as the partition key and order_timestamp as the sort key.","Create a local secondary index (LSI) with product_id as the sort key.","Run a Scan operation with a FilterExpression on product_id.","Have the application write a copy of every order into a second table keyed by product_id."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah tabel 'already in production', pola akses baru berdasarkan 'product_id' (atribut yang bukan partition key), dan 'eventually consistent reads are acceptable'. Global secondary index (GSI) boleh memiliki partition key yang berbeda dari tabel dasar, dapat ditambahkan kapan saja ke tabel yang sudah ada, dan dipelihara otomatis oleh DynamoDB; GSI hanya mendukung eventually consistent read, yang memang dapat diterima. Distraktor terdekat adalah LSI: LSI harus memakai partition key yang sama (customer_id) dan hanya dapat dibuat saat tabel dibuat, sehingga tidak bisa melayani query per product_id. Scan membaca seluruh 2 TB lalu memfilter, sangat mahal dan lambat. Tabel kedua yang ditulis aplikasi menambah kode dan risiko inkonsistensi. Aturan umum: pola akses baru dengan partition key berbeda pada tabel yang sudah ada → GSI.","r":["Benar — GSI mendukung partition key berbeda, bisa ditambahkan ke tabel yang sudah ada, dan cocok jika eventual consistency dapat diterima.","Salah — LSI wajib memakai partition key yang sama dan hanya bisa dibuat saat pembuatan tabel.","Salah — Scan membaca seluruh tabel dan mengonsumsi kapasitas besar; FilterExpression tidak mengurangi data yang dibaca.","Salah — Menulis ganda dari aplikasi menambah overhead dan risiko data tidak sinkron, padahal GSI melakukannya otomatis."],"k":"New access pattern on different partition key, existing table → GSI. LSI = same partition key, only at table creation."},{"id":"E1B-47","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Troubleshooting data skew in Spark","q":"A Spark job on Amazon EMR joins a large orders dataset with a customers dataset on customer_id. Most stages complete quickly, but one stage runs for hours because a few tasks process far more data than the others. The Spark UI shows that a small number of customer_id values account for most of the orders. Which solution will MOST improve job performance?","o":["Increase the number of core nodes in the cluster.","Increase the executor memory so that the largest tasks do not spill to disk.","Change the output format from Parquet to CSV.","Mitigate the data skew by salting the hot join keys (or enabling Spark adaptive query execution skew-join handling) so the large keys are split across many tasks."],"a":[3],"e":"Gejala kuncinya adalah 'a few tasks process far more data than the others' dan 'a small number of customer_id values account for most of the orders', yang merupakan ciri data skew. Karena semua baris dengan kunci yang sama dikirim ke satu partisi, menambah node tidak membantu: task panas itu tetap dijalankan oleh satu core. Salting (menambahkan suffix acak ke kunci panas dan mereplikasi sisi kecil) atau fitur skew-join pada Spark adaptive query execution membagi kunci besar ke banyak task sehingga beban merata. Menambah memori executor dapat mengurangi spill, tetapi task tersebut tetap berjalan sendirian dan lama. Mengubah format output tidak berkaitan dengan tahap join. Aturan umum: straggler task karena distribusi kunci tidak merata → atasi skew (salting, AQE, broadcast join jika sisi kecil cukup kecil).","r":["Salah — Node tambahan tidak membantu karena kunci panas tetap diproses oleh satu task.","Salah — Mengurangi spill, tetapi tidak membagi beban task yang terlalu besar.","Salah — Format output tidak memengaruhi stage join yang lambat.","Benar — Salting atau AQE skew join memecah kunci panas ke banyak task sehingga beban merata."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'few straggler tasks + uneven key distribution' → data skew → salting/AQE, bukan tambah node."},{"id":"E2A-47","d":2,"ts":"2.1.6","t":"Redshift transactions and TRUNCATE","q":"A data engineer must fully replace the contents of an Amazon Redshift reporting table every night. Dashboards query the table continuously, and users must never see an empty or partially loaded table. The engineer writes the following steps inside a single transaction: BEGIN; then remove existing rows; then INSERT INTO sales_report SELECT ... FROM staging; then END. Which statement should be used to remove the existing rows?","o":["TRUNCATE sales_report;","DROP TABLE sales_report; followed by CREATE TABLE sales_report;","DELETE FROM sales_report;","VACUUM DELETE ONLY sales_report;"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'users must never see an empty or partially loaded table' dan semua langkah berada 'inside a single transaction'. Di Amazon Redshift, TRUNCATE melakukan commit implisit terhadap transaksi yang sedang berjalan, sehingga pengguna dashboard bisa melihat tabel kosong sebelum INSERT selesai. DELETE FROM tetap berada di dalam transaksi: pembaca terus melihat versi data lama (snapshot) sampai END/COMMIT, kemudian langsung melihat data baru secara atomik. Distraktor terdekat adalah TRUNCATE: lebih cepat dan tidak meninggalkan baris terhapus yang perlu di-VACUUM, tetapi justru melanggar syarat atomisitas. DROP/CREATE juga melepas tabel sementara dan menghapus izin. VACUUM tidak menghapus baris yang masih aktif. Aturan umum: penggantian data atomik di Redshift → DELETE di dalam transaksi (atau staging table + ALTER TABLE APPEND/rename), hindari TRUNCATE karena commit implisit.","r":["Salah — TRUNCATE melakukan commit implisit di Redshift sehingga dashboard dapat melihat tabel kosong sebelum INSERT selesai.","Salah — DROP dan CREATE membuat tabel hilang sementara, menghapus grant, dan dapat memutus view yang bergantung padanya.","Benar — DELETE tetap berada di dalam transaksi sehingga pembaca melihat data lama sampai commit, lalu data baru secara atomik.","Salah — VACUUM hanya mereklamasi ruang dari baris yang sudah dihapus; ia tidak menghapus baris aktif."],"k":"Redshift: TRUNCATE commits implicitly → for atomic reload inside a transaction use DELETE."},{"id":"E1C-15","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Lambda Kinesis error handling","q":"An AWS Lambda function consumes an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream through an event source mapping. A single malformed record causes the function to throw an exception, and the whole shard stops progressing while the batch is retried until the record expires. The team wants the shard to keep moving and to keep the bad records for later analysis. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable BisectBatchOnFunctionError on the event source mapping.","Increase the number of shards in the stream.","Set MaximumRetryAttempts (or MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds) on the event source mapping and configure an on-failure destination such as an Amazon SQS queue.","Increase the Lambda function memory to 10,240 MB.","Set the function's reserved concurrency to 0."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Masalahnya: satu 'malformed record' memblokir shard karena secara default Lambda mengulang batch dari Kinesis sampai record kedaluwarsa. BisectBatchOnFunctionError membelah batch yang gagal menjadi dua dan mencoba ulang secara terpisah, sehingga record bermasalah terisolasi dan record yang sehat tetap diproses. MaximumRetryAttempts atau MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds membatasi pengulangan, dan on-failure destination (SQS/SNS) menyimpan metadata batch yang gagal untuk analisis, lalu shard bergerak lagi. Distractor terdekat adalah menambah shard: tidak menghilangkan record buruk, sehingga shard yang berisi record itu tetap macet. Menambah memori tidak memperbaiki exception dari data salah, dan reserved concurrency 0 justru menghentikan semua pemrosesan. Aturan umum: poison record pada stream → bisect batch + batas retry + on-failure destination.","r":["Benar — Bisect batch mengisolasi record bermasalah sehingga record lain dalam batch tetap berhasil diproses.","Salah — Shard baru tidak menghapus record buruk di shard yang sudah ada.","Benar — Batas retry/usia record menghentikan pengulangan tak berujung, dan destinasi on-failure menyimpan info batch gagal.","Salah — Memori tidak memperbaiki exception akibat data yang salah format.","Salah — Concurrency 0 men-throttle seluruh fungsi sehingga tidak ada record yang diproses."],"k":"Tips ujian: Kinesis + Lambda 'poison pill' → BisectBatchOnFunctionError + MaximumRetryAttempts + on-failure destination."},{"id":"E3B-60","d":3,"ts":"3.4.4","t":"Stratified sampling","q":"A data scientist needs a 1% sample of 2 billion card transactions to explore fraud patterns. Only 0.1% of transactions are fraudulent, and fraud rates differ greatly between 12 regions. The sample must preserve the proportion of fraudulent transactions in every region so that no region or class is under-represented. Which sampling technique should the data engineer use?","o":["Simple random sampling of 1% of all rows.","Stratified sampling that samples 1% within each region and fraud-label combination.","Taking the first 1% of rows ordered by transaction time.","Cluster sampling that selects 1% of the days and keeps all transactions from those days."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'preserve the proportion of fraudulent transactions in every region' dengan kelas yang sangat jarang (0.1%). Stratified sampling membagi populasi ke dalam strata (di sini region × label fraud) lalu mengambil sampel dari setiap strata dengan proporsi yang ditentukan, sehingga setiap kelompok terwakili sesuai proporsinya. Distraktor terdekat adalah simple random sampling: rata-rata proporsinya benar, tetapi untuk kelas yang sangat jarang dan region kecil, variasi acak bisa membuat sebagian kelompok kurang terwakili atau tidak muncul sama sekali. Mengambil 1% pertama berdasarkan waktu bias ke periode awal. Cluster sampling per hari bisa melewatkan pola region tertentu. Aturan: harus menjaga proporsi subkelompok → stratified sampling.","r":["Salah — Sampel acak sederhana tidak menjamin kelas jarang di setiap region terwakili.","Benar — Stratified sampling menjaga proporsi per region dan label fraud.","Salah — Sampel berdasarkan urutan waktu bias ke periode tertentu.","Salah — Memilih hari tertentu bisa melewatkan variasi region dan menambah korelasi dalam cluster."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'preserve proportions of subgroups / rare class' → stratified sampling."},{"id":"E2A-60","d":2,"ts":"2.1.8","t":"Vector index concepts","q":"A data engineer is explaining vector index types to a team that will use vector search in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL and Amazon OpenSearch Service. Which TWO statements are correct? (Choose TWO.)","o":["HNSW search quality can be raised at query time by increasing the ef_search parameter, at the cost of higher query latency.","IVF indexes do not require any training or clustering step before vectors are added.","HNSW indexes always return exact nearest neighbors, so they have 100% recall.","IVF indexes partition vectors into clusters around centroids and search only the nearest clusters, which uses less memory than HNSW but can reduce recall.","A Flat index is an approximate index that trades accuracy for speed."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Soal ini menguji pemahaman konsep index vektor. HNSW adalah index approximate berbasis graph; parameter ef_search (di pgvector hnsw.ef_search, di OpenSearch ef_search, di MemoryDB EF_RUNTIME) mengatur ukuran daftar kandidat saat pencarian, sehingga menaikkannya meningkatkan recall dengan biaya latensi. IVF membagi ruang vektor ke cluster di sekitar centroid hasil training/clustering, lalu hanya mencari di sejumlah cluster terdekat (probes/nprobes); ini lebih hemat memori tetapi dapat menurunkan recall. Distraktor terdekat adalah 'HNSW always returns exact nearest neighbors': HNSW tetap approximate sehingga recall bisa di bawah 100%. IVF justru memerlukan langkah training/clustering. Flat adalah pencarian eksak brute-force, bukan approximate. Aturan umum: Flat = eksak dan lambat; HNSW = approximate, cepat, recall tinggi, boros memori; IVF = approximate, hemat memori, perlu training.","r":["Benar — Menaikkan ef_search memperluas pencarian graph HNSW sehingga recall naik dengan latensi lebih tinggi.","Salah — IVF memerlukan training atau clustering untuk menentukan centroid sebelum vektor diindeks.","Salah — HNSW adalah algoritme approximate nearest neighbor sehingga recall tidak dijamin 100%.","Benar — IVF mencari hanya di cluster terdekat, lebih hemat memori daripada HNSW tetapi dapat menurunkan recall.","Salah — Flat index melakukan pencarian brute-force yang eksak, bukan approximate."],"k":"Flat = exact/slow; HNSW = graph, fast, high recall, more memory, tune ef_search; IVF = clusters, less memory, needs training, tune probes."},{"id":"E3A-36","d":3,"ts":"3.1.9","t":"EventBridge Pipes","q":"Order events arrive in an Amazon SQS queue. Only events where the order total is greater than 1,000 must start an AWS Step Functions workflow, and each event must first be enriched with customer details returned by an AWS Lambda function. The data engineer wants a point-to-point integration without writing polling or routing code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write an AWS Lambda function that polls the queue, filters the events, calls the enrichment function, and starts the workflow.","Configure the SQS queue to publish to an Amazon SNS topic with a subscription filter policy that targets Step Functions.","Create an Amazon EventBridge Pipe with the SQS queue as the source, an event filter for order total greater than 1,000, the Lambda function as the enrichment step, and the state machine as the target.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule on the default event bus that reads directly from the SQS queue."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'SQS source', 'filter', 'enrichment', 'Step Functions target', dan 'point-to-point integration without polling code'. Amazon EventBridge Pipes menghubungkan satu source ke satu target dengan tahap opsional filtering dan enrichment. Pipe mem-poll SQS secara terkelola, memfilter dengan event pattern (numeric filter untuk total di atas 1.000), memperkaya dengan Lambda, lalu memulai state machine. Lambda kustom berfungsi tetapi justru menjadi kode polling dan routing yang ingin dihindari. SQS tidak bisa mem-publish ke SNS, dan SNS juga tidak memiliki subscription langsung ke Step Functions. Rule EventBridge bereaksi pada event di event bus dan tidak bisa membaca langsung dari queue SQS. Aturan umum: source ke target dengan filter dan enrichment → EventBridge Pipes; routing banyak ke banyak → event bus + rules.","r":["Salah — Ini adalah kode polling dan routing kustom yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — SQS tidak bisa mem-publish ke SNS, dan SNS tidak memiliki target langsung Step Functions.","Benar — EventBridge Pipes menyediakan source SQS, filter, enrichment Lambda, dan target Step Functions tanpa kode polling.","Salah — Rule EventBridge tidak membaca pesan dari queue SQS."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'source → filter → enrich → target, point-to-point' → EventBridge Pipes."},{"id":"E1A-23","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"Amazon AppFlow incremental transfer","q":"A company uses Amazon AppFlow to copy records from a ServiceNow instance to Amazon S3 every hour. Each run currently transfers all records, which takes a long time and consumes the SaaS API quota. The company wants each run to transfer only records that were created or modified since the last run. What should the data engineer configure?","o":["Change the flow to run on demand and trigger it manually.","Replace AppFlow with AWS DataSync.","Add a filter in AppFlow that excludes records older than one year.","Configure the scheduled flow to use incremental transfer based on a timestamp field such as the last-updated date."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only records that were created or modified since the last run' dan masalah 'API quota'. Flow terjadwal di Amazon AppFlow mendukung mode incremental transfer yang memakai field timestamp (misalnya tanggal last-updated) sehingga setiap run hanya menarik record baru atau berubah sejak run sebelumnya. Ini mengurangi waktu transfer dan pemakaian kuota API. Distraktor terdekat adalah filter 'lebih tua dari satu tahun': tetap menarik banyak record yang tidak berubah setiap jam. Mengubah ke on-demand tidak mengurangi volume per run dan menambah kerja manual. DataSync tidak dapat membaca data dari API SaaS. Aturan umum: AppFlow terjadwal + hanya perubahan = incremental transfer berdasarkan field timestamp.","r":["Salah — On-demand tetap mentransfer semua record dan menambah langkah manual.","Salah — DataSync memindahkan file dari storage, bukan data dari API SaaS.","Salah — Filter umur tetap menarik record yang tidak berubah setiap run.","Benar — Incremental transfer berbasis timestamp hanya menarik record baru atau berubah."],"k":"AppFlow terjadwal, hanya data baru/berubah → incremental transfer (timestamp field)."},{"id":"E3A-59","d":3,"ts":"3.2.5","t":"Redshift provisioned vs Serverless cost","q":"A company runs Amazon Redshift for BI dashboards that are used 24 hours a day by teams in several time zones. Query load is steady and predictable, and the company has committed to this workload for at least 3 years. The company wants the LOWEST cost for this workload. Which option should the data engineer choose?","o":["Amazon Redshift Serverless with a high base capacity.","Amazon Athena with the data stored in Amazon S3.","Amazon Redshift Serverless with a low maximum RPU limit.","An Amazon Redshift provisioned RA3 cluster sized for the steady load, purchased with reserved nodes for a 3-year term."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'used 24 hours a day', 'steady and predictable', 'committed for at least 3 years', dan 'LOWEST cost'. Untuk beban yang stabil dan selalu aktif, cluster provisioned yang ukurannya sesuai beban akan terpakai tinggi sepanjang waktu, dan reserved nodes untuk jangka 3 tahun memberi diskon besar dibandingkan on-demand. Redshift Serverless ditagih per RPU-hour saat ada query berjalan; untuk beban 24/7 tagihan berjalan hampir terus-menerus tanpa keuntungan auto-pause, sehingga biasanya lebih mahal dibandingkan provisioned yang direservasi. Membatasi max RPU di Serverless menghemat biaya tetapi bisa menurunkan performa dashboard. Athena adalah query engine atas data di S3, bukan data warehouse untuk beban dashboard Redshift yang sudah ada; memindahkan beban ini berarti migrasi besar dan, dengan tagihan per data yang dipindai, biaya ribuan query dashboard sepanjang hari bisa tinggi. Aturan umum: beban steady 24/7 + komitmen jangka panjang → provisioned + reserved; beban sporadis atau tidak terduga → serverless.","r":["Salah — Serverless untuk beban 24/7 hampir selalu ditagih dan tidak mendapat diskon komitmen seperti reserved nodes.","Salah — Memindahkan beban dari Redshift ke Athena adalah migrasi besar, dan biaya per data yang dipindai untuk query dashboard terus-menerus bisa tinggi.","Salah — Batas RPU rendah dapat memperlambat dashboard dan tetap tidak memberi diskon jangka panjang.","Benar — Cluster provisioned dengan reserved nodes 3 tahun paling murah untuk beban stabil yang selalu aktif."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'steady, predictable, 24/7, long-term' → provisioned + reserved; 'intermittent/unpredictable' → serverless."},{"id":"E4A-37","d":4,"ts":"4.2.2","t":"Secrets Manager replica secrets","q":"A company runs its data pipelines in us-east-1 and maintains a warm standby copy in us-west-2 for disaster recovery. Pipelines in both Regions connect to Amazon Aurora global database clusters by using credentials stored in AWS Secrets Manager in us-east-1, with automatic rotation every 30 days. During a Regional outage, the standby pipelines must still be able to retrieve the current credentials with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Configure the secret as a multi-Region secret by replicating it to us-west-2, and have the standby pipelines read the replica in us-west-2.","Create a second secret in us-west-2 and use a scheduled Lambda function to copy the value after each rotation.","Export the secret value to an Amazon S3 bucket with Cross-Region Replication to us-west-2.","Store a copy of the credentials as a SecureString parameter in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store in us-west-2 and update it manually after each rotation."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'Regional outage', 'current credentials', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Secrets Manager mendukung replikasi secret ke Region lain: replica secret selalu disinkronkan dengan primary, termasuk nilai baru setelah rotasi, dan aplikasi di Region sekunder bisa membacanya secara lokal. Jika Region primary bermasalah, replica dapat dipromosikan menjadi secret mandiri. Menyalin nilai dengan Lambda terjadwal atau secara manual menambah overhead dan berisiko ada jeda ketika nilai belum tersinkron. Mengekspor secret ke S3 menyimpan password di luar layanan secret dan memperluas permukaan kebocoran. Aturan umum: credential untuk DR multi-Region → Secrets Manager replica secrets.","r":["Benar — Replica secret disinkronkan otomatis termasuk hasil rotasi dan dapat dibaca di Region sekunder.","Salah — Sinkronisasi custom menambah overhead dan bisa tertinggal setelah rotasi.","Salah — Menyimpan password di S3 tidak aman dan bukan pola yang direkomendasikan.","Salah — Update manual rawan lupa dan menambah overhead operasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: secret yang sama dibutuhkan di beberapa Region untuk DR → Secrets Manager multi-Region replication."},{"id":"E4A-14","d":4,"ts":"4.1.4","t":"API Gateway service integration role","q":"A company wants mobile devices to send clickstream events through an Amazon API Gateway REST API directly to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams by using an AWS service integration, without any Lambda function in between. What must a data engineer configure so that API Gateway is authorized to write to the stream?","o":["Add a resource-based policy to the Kinesis data stream that allows any principal to call kinesis:PutRecord.","Create an API key and a usage plan, and attach them to the API stage.","Configure an Amazon Cognito user pool authorizer on the API method.","Create an IAM role that trusts apigateway.amazonaws.com and allows kinesis:PutRecord on the stream, and specify the role ARN as the credentials of the integration request."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'AWS service integration' dan 'API Gateway is authorized to write to the stream'. Pada integrasi langsung ke service AWS, API Gateway sendiri yang memanggil API Kinesis, sehingga ia membutuhkan IAM role yang bisa di-assume (trust apigateway.amazonaws.com) dengan permission kinesis:PutRecord atau PutRecords pada stream tersebut. ARN role ini diisi di bagian credentials pada integration request. API key dan usage plan hanya untuk throttling dan identifikasi klien, bukan otorisasi ke backend. Cognito authorizer mengautentikasi pemanggil API, tetapi tidak memberi API Gateway hak menulis ke Kinesis. Resource policy yang mengizinkan semua principal sangat tidak aman. Aturan umum: bedakan autentikasi klien ke API (IAM/Cognito/Lambda authorizer) dan otorisasi API Gateway ke backend (integration role).","r":["Salah — Mengizinkan semua principal menulis ke stream melanggar least privilege dan bukan cara standar integrasi API Gateway.","Salah — API key dan usage plan mengatur kuota dan throttling, bukan izin akses ke Kinesis.","Salah — Cognito authorizer mengautentikasi klien, bukan memberi API Gateway izin memanggil Kinesis.","Benar — Integration role yang di-assume API Gateway memberi izin kinesis:PutRecord secara terbatas pada stream."],"k":"Tips ujian: API Gateway langsung ke service AWS (Kinesis, SQS, DynamoDB) → integration request credentials = IAM role yang trust apigateway.amazonaws.com."},{"id":"E1A-34","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"Redshift scheduled queries","q":"An analytics team wants a SQL statement that refreshes a summary table in an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster to run every morning at 06:00. The team prefers the simplest solution and does not want to write or deploy any code. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a scheduled query in Amazon Redshift Query Editor v2.","Write an AWS Lambda function that connects through JDBC and schedule it with EventBridge.","Deploy an Amazon MWAA environment with a DAG that runs the SQL statement.","Run the statement from an Amazon EC2 instance using crontab and psql."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: menjalankan 'a SQL statement' di Redshift setiap pagi, 'simplest solution', dan 'does not want to write or deploy any code'. Redshift Query Editor v2 mendukung scheduled query: Anda memilih query, menetapkan jadwal, dan Redshift memakai EventBridge serta Redshift Data API di belakang layar. Tidak ada kode atau infrastruktur tambahan. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda + EventBridge: berfungsi, tetapi memerlukan penulisan dan deployment kode. MWAA berlebihan untuk satu query, dan EC2 dengan crontab menambah server. Aturan umum: SQL terjadwal di Redshift tanpa kode = scheduled query di Query Editor v2.","r":["Benar — Scheduled query di Query Editor v2 menjadwalkan SQL tanpa menulis kode.","Salah — Memerlukan penulisan dan deployment kode Lambda serta pengelolaan driver.","Salah — MWAA berlebihan dan mahal untuk satu query terjadwal.","Salah — EC2 dengan crontab menambah server yang harus dikelola."],"k":"SQL Redshift terjadwal tanpa kode → Query Editor v2 scheduled query."},{"id":"E4A-01","d":4,"ts":"4.1.1","t":"Glue connection security group self-referencing rule","q":"A data engineer creates an AWS Glue JDBC connection to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database in a private subnet. When the Glue ETL job starts, it fails with the error 'At least one security group must open all ingress ports. To limit traffic, the source security group in your inbound rule can be restricted to the same security group.' The RDS security group already allows TCP 5432 from the Glue connection's security group. Which change will resolve the error while keeping access restricted?","o":["Add an inbound rule to the Glue connection's security group that allows TCP 5432 from 0.0.0.0/0.","Add a self-referencing inbound rule to the Glue connection's security group that allows all TCP traffic from the same security group.","Add an inbound rule to the subnet's network ACL that allows all TCP traffic from the VPC CIDR range.","Attach an internet gateway to the VPC and move the Glue connection to a public subnet."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci di pesan error-nya sendiri: 'source security group ... restricted to the same security group'. AWS Glue membuat beberapa elastic network interface (ENI) untuk worker Spark di subnet tersebut, dan worker-worker itu harus bisa saling berkomunikasi di semua port TCP. Karena itu security group yang dipakai Glue connection wajib punya inbound rule self-referencing (source = security group itu sendiri) untuk semua port TCP. Rule ini tetap ketat karena hanya ENI yang memakai security group yang sama yang bisa masuk. Membuka 5432 dari 0.0.0.0/0 tidak menyelesaikan kebutuhan komunikasi antar-worker dan malah memperlebar akses. Network ACL bukan pengganti security group, dan internet gateway tidak relevan untuk koneksi privat ke RDS. Aturan umum: Glue connection di VPC = security group dengan self-referencing rule all TCP, plus akses S3 lewat gateway endpoint atau NAT.","r":["Salah — Membuka port 5432 ke seluruh internet melanggar prinsip akses terbatas dan tidak memenuhi syarat Glue bahwa worker harus bisa saling terhubung di semua port.","Benar — Self-referencing rule all TCP memenuhi syarat Glue untuk komunikasi antar-ENI worker, dan aksesnya tetap terbatas hanya ke resource dengan security group yang sama.","Salah — Network ACL bersifat stateless dan dievaluasi terpisah; Glue tetap memvalidasi rule di security group sehingga error tidak hilang.","Salah — Internet gateway dan subnet publik tidak diperlukan untuk akses ke RDS privat dan justru menambah eksposur."],"k":"Tips ujian: error Glue 'security group must open all ingress ports' → tambahkan self-referencing inbound rule all TCP pada security group Glue connection."},{"id":"E2A-24","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Purpose-built databases: Keyspaces","q":"A company runs a 30-node Apache Cassandra cluster on Amazon EC2 for a time-series messaging application that uses CQL. The operations team spends significant time on patching, node replacement, and capacity planning. The company wants a serverless option that keeps the existing CQL code and drivers. Which data store should a data engineer recommend?","o":["Amazon DynamoDB with the application rewritten to use the DynamoDB SDK","Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra)","Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)","Amazon MemoryDB"],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'Apache Cassandra', 'CQL', 'serverless', dan 'keeps the existing CQL code and drivers'. Amazon Keyspaces adalah layanan serverless yang kompatibel dengan Apache Cassandra, mendukung CQL dan driver Cassandra yang sudah ada, serta mengelola patching, replikasi, dan scaling otomatis. Distraktor terdekat adalah DynamoDB: serverless dan sangat skalabel, tetapi aplikasi harus ditulis ulang ke API DynamoDB, melanggar syarat mempertahankan kode CQL. DocumentDB kompatibel dengan MongoDB, bukan Cassandra. MemoryDB adalah database in-memory kompatibel Redis/Valkey. Aturan umum: Cassandra/CQL + managed/serverless → Amazon Keyspaces.","r":["Salah — Menulis ulang aplikasi ke DynamoDB SDK bertentangan dengan syarat mempertahankan kode CQL.","Benar — Keyspaces kompatibel dengan CQL dan driver Cassandra serta serverless, menghilangkan beban operasional cluster.","Salah — DocumentDB memakai API MongoDB, tidak kompatibel dengan CQL.","Salah — MemoryDB kompatibel dengan Redis/Valkey, bukan Cassandra, dan menyimpan data in-memory yang mahal untuk time-series besar."],"k":"Cassandra / CQL → Amazon Keyspaces (serverless)."},{"id":"E1B-24","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Redshift federated query vs zero-ETL","q":"Analysts run all of their reports in an Amazon Redshift data warehouse. They now need to join live customer status data from an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database with historical sales tables in Redshift. A data residency policy prohibits copying or replicating the operational customer data into Redshift storage. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Redshift federated queries by creating an external schema that points to the Aurora PostgreSQL database.","Configure an Aurora zero-ETL integration with Amazon Redshift.","Use AWS DMS with ongoing replication from Aurora PostgreSQL to Redshift.","Run a nightly AWS Glue job that copies the customer tables from Aurora PostgreSQL into Redshift."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci penentunya adalah 'live customer status data', laporan yang tetap dijalankan di Redshift, dan larangan 'copying or replicating the operational customer data into Redshift storage'. Redshift federated query memungkinkan query SQL di Redshift membaca langsung dari Aurora/RDS PostgreSQL (dan MySQL) melalui external schema, sehingga data operasional tetap berada di Aurora dan hasilnya selalu terkini. Zero-ETL integration adalah distraktor terdekat karena memberi data hampir real-time tanpa pipeline, tetapi zero-ETL mereplikasi data ke Redshift sehingga melanggar kebijakan. DMS replikasi berkelanjutan juga menyalin data, dan Glue nightly menyalin data serta tidak live. Aturan umum: query data operasional secara live dari Redshift tanpa memindahkan data → federated query; replikasi tanpa pipeline → zero-ETL.","r":["Benar — Federated query membaca data Aurora secara langsung dan live tanpa menyimpannya di Redshift.","Salah — Zero-ETL mereplikasi data ke Redshift, sehingga melanggar larangan penyalinan.","Salah — DMS ongoing replication menyalin data ke Redshift.","Salah — Glue nightly menyalin data dan tidak memberikan data live."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'query live RDS/Aurora data from Redshift without moving it' → Redshift federated query; 'replicate without ETL' → zero-ETL."},{"id":"E1A-12","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"Redshift UNLOAD","q":"A data science team uses Apache Spark on Amazon EMR and needs a monthly snapshot of several large Amazon Redshift tables in Amazon S3. The files must be in a columnar format and partitioned by month to minimize scan costs. Which approach should the data engineer use?","o":["Run SELECT queries through the Redshift JDBC driver from the EMR cluster and write the result set to Amazon S3 as CSV.","Take a manual snapshot of the Redshift cluster and share the snapshot with the data science account.","Use the Redshift UNLOAD command with FORMAT AS PARQUET and PARTITION BY on the month column to write the data to Amazon S3.","Use AWS DMS to replicate the Redshift tables to Amazon S3 as CSV files."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'columnar format' dan 'partitioned by month'. Perintah UNLOAD di Redshift mengekspor hasil query secara paralel dari semua slice langsung ke S3, mendukung FORMAT AS PARQUET dan PARTITION BY sehingga hasilnya hemat untuk discan oleh Spark atau Athena. Distraktor terdekat adalah membaca lewat JDBC: semua data melewati leader node satu koneksi sehingga lambat untuk tabel besar, dan CSV bukan format kolumnar. Snapshot cluster adalah backup Redshift, bukan file yang bisa dibaca Spark. DMS dirancang untuk migrasi/replikasi database operasional, bukan ekspor analitik dari Redshift, dan CSV tidak memenuhi syarat kolumnar. Aturan umum: ekspor massal dari Redshift ke data lake = UNLOAD (Parquet + PARTITION BY).","r":["Salah — JDBC menarik data melalui leader node sehingga lambat, dan CSV bukan format kolumnar.","Salah — Snapshot Redshift adalah backup cluster, tidak bisa dibaca langsung oleh Spark di EMR.","Benar — UNLOAD mengekspor paralel ke S3 dalam Parquet dengan partisi per bulan.","Salah — DMS bukan alat yang tepat untuk ekspor snapshot analitik dari Redshift, dan CSV tidak kolumnar."],"k":"Redshift → S3 bulk, kolumnar, terpartisi → UNLOAD ... FORMAT AS PARQUET PARTITION BY."},{"id":"E4A-24","d":4,"ts":"4.1.6","t":"EMR on EC2 vs Glue responsibilities","q":"A company is deciding between running Apache Spark ETL on Amazon EMR on EC2 clusters or on AWS Glue. The security team asks which security tasks the data team would own with EMR on EC2 that AWS handles for it with AWS Glue. Which TWO tasks meet this description? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Keeping the operating system of the cluster instances patched by relaunching clusters with updated Amazon EMR releases or AMIs.","Defining IAM permissions that allow the Spark jobs to read source data from Amazon S3.","Managing EC2 key pairs and controlling SSH access to the cluster nodes.","Encrypting the output data that the jobs write to Amazon S3.","Physically securing the servers in the AWS data centers."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: tugas yang dimiliki data team di EMR on EC2 tetapi ditangani AWS di Glue. EMR on EC2 berjalan di instance EC2 di akun Anda, sehingga Anda bertanggung jawab memperbarui OS (dengan me-launch cluster memakai rilis EMR atau AMI terbaru) dan mengelola akses ke node seperti key pair dan SSH. AWS Glue adalah serverless dan managed; tidak ada instance atau SSH yang Anda kelola, dan AWS yang mem-patch lingkungan eksekusi. Sebaliknya, IAM permission untuk akses S3 dan enkripsi output tetap tanggung jawab pelanggan di kedua opsi. Keamanan fisik data center selalu tanggung jawab AWS. Aturan umum: unmanaged/semi-managed (EC2, EMR on EC2) menambah tanggung jawab OS dan akses host; managed/serverless (Glue, Athena) menghapusnya.","r":["Benar — Pada EMR on EC2, pelanggan harus memastikan cluster memakai rilis/AMI terbaru; di Glue, AWS yang mengelola patching.","Salah — IAM permission untuk akses data tetap tanggung jawab pelanggan di EMR maupun Glue.","Benar — Key pair dan SSH ke node hanya relevan di EMR on EC2; Glue tidak mengekspos host.","Salah — Konfigurasi enkripsi output tetap tanggung jawab pelanggan di kedua service.","Salah — Keamanan fisik selalu tanggung jawab AWS di kedua service."],"k":"Tips ujian: managed vs unmanaged → OS patching dan akses host pindah ke AWS; IAM, enkripsi, dan data tetap milik pelanggan."},{"id":"E2B-48","d":2,"ts":"2.3.4","t":"S3 Versioning for recovery","q":"A nightly AWS Glue job writes curated CSV files to the same S3 keys every night. Last week a bug in the job overwrote a month of curated data with empty files, and the data could not be recovered. The company wants to be able to restore the previous content of any overwritten or deleted object with the LEAST operational overhead. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Enable S3 Object Lock in compliance mode on the bucket.","Enable S3 Versioning on the bucket and use Lifecycle rules to expire noncurrent versions after a defined retention period.","Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication to a bucket in another Region without versioning.","Copy the bucket to another bucket once a week with S3 Batch Operations."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'overwrote', 'restore the previous content of any overwritten or deleted object' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. S3 Versioning menyimpan setiap versi objek, sehingga overwrite membuat versi baru dan versi lama tetap ada; penghapusan hanya menambahkan delete marker yang bisa dihapus untuk memulihkan objek. Lifecycle NoncurrentVersionExpiration menjaga biaya tetap terkendali. Object Lock compliance mencegah overwrite versi yang dilindungi, tetapi terlalu ketat dan menghalangi job yang sah memperbarui data. Replication membutuhkan versioning di kedua bucket, dan replikasi juga menyalin overwrite yang buruk. Salinan mingguan bisa kehilangan data hingga 7 hari. Ingat: 'recover from accidental overwrite/delete' → S3 Versioning (+ lifecycle untuk noncurrent).","r":["Salah — Compliance mode mencegah perubahan sah dan tidak bisa dibatalkan, jadi terlalu kaku untuk kebutuhan rollback.","Benar — Versioning menyimpan versi sebelumnya untuk dipulihkan, dan lifecycle mengendalikan biaya versi lama.","Salah — CRR membutuhkan versioning dan juga mereplikasi overwrite yang rusak.","Salah — Salinan mingguan memberi RPO hingga 7 hari dan menambah biaya serta pekerjaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'accidental overwrite or delete' → enable S3 Versioning."},{"id":"E4B-13","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"S3 DSSE-KMS","q":"A government contractor stores classified project files in Amazon S3. A new compliance standard requires that the objects be protected by two independent layers of server-side encryption at rest, and the company wants AWS to manage the encryption process. Which S3 encryption option meets this requirement?","o":["Server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3)","Server-side encryption with customer-provided keys (SSE-C)","Server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) with S3 Bucket Keys enabled","Dual-layer server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (DSSE-KMS)"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'two independent layers of server-side encryption at rest'. DSSE-KMS (dual-layer server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys) menerapkan dua lapisan enkripsi independen pada objek di sisi server dan dirancang untuk memenuhi standar kepatuhan yang mensyaratkan multilayer encryption. Kunci tetap dikelola melalui AWS KMS sehingga penggunaannya teraudit di CloudTrail. Distraktor terdekat adalah SSE-KMS dengan Bucket Keys: tetap hanya satu lapisan enkripsi; Bucket Keys hanya mengurangi panggilan KMS. SSE-S3 juga satu lapisan. SSE-C membuat pelanggan harus mengirim dan mengelola kunci di setiap request, dan tetap satu lapisan. Aturan umum: 'dual-layer/multilayer encryption at rest di S3' → DSSE-KMS.","r":["Salah — SSE-S3 hanya menyediakan satu lapisan enkripsi.","Salah — SSE-C hanya satu lapisan dan pelanggan harus mengelola serta mengirim kunci di setiap request.","Salah — Bucket Keys mengurangi biaya KMS tetapi enkripsi tetap satu lapisan.","Benar — DSSE-KMS menerapkan dua lapisan enkripsi server-side yang independen dengan kunci KMS."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'two layers of encryption' untuk objek S3 → DSSE-KMS."},{"id":"E2A-35","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"AWS DataSync","q":"A company has 200 TB of research data on an on-premises NFS file server. The company has a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect link. It needs to copy all the data to Amazon S3 within 2 weeks and then keep S3 updated every night with new and changed files until the data center closes in 6 months. Data integrity must be verified automatically. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Deploy an AWS DataSync agent on premises, create a task from the NFS share to Amazon S3, and schedule it to run nightly.","Order AWS Snowball Edge devices for the initial copy and use the AWS CLI s3 sync command nightly.","Create an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server and have the file server push files to it nightly.","Write a script that runs the AWS CLI s3 cp command nightly on an on-premises server."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'on-premises NFS', '10 Gbps Direct Connect', salinan awal 200 TB dalam '2 weeks', sinkronisasi 'every night with new and changed files', dan 'data integrity must be verified automatically'. AWS DataSync memakai agent on-premises untuk menyalin dari NFS/SMB/HDFS ke S3, EFS, atau FSx, dengan transfer paralel yang cepat, hanya menyalin data yang berubah pada eksekusi berikutnya, penjadwalan bawaan, dan verifikasi integritas otomatis. Dengan 10 Gbps, 200 TB dapat ditransfer dalam beberapa hari. Distraktor terdekat adalah Snowball Edge + s3 sync: Snowball cocok bila bandwidth terbatas, tetapi di sini jaringan cukup, dan skrip CLI menambah pekerjaan serta tidak memberi verifikasi integritas terkelola. Transfer Family ditujukan untuk pertukaran file dengan pihak eksternal, bukan migrasi file server. Aturan umum: migrasi/sinkronisasi online NFS/SMB ke AWS dengan jadwal → DataSync.","r":["Benar — DataSync menangani salinan awal dan sinkronisasi inkremental terjadwal dengan verifikasi integritas otomatis melalui Direct Connect.","Salah — Snowball tidak perlu karena bandwidth cukup, dan skrip s3 sync menambah overhead serta tidak memberi verifikasi terkelola.","Salah — Transfer Family dirancang untuk pertukaran file dengan partner, bukan sinkronisasi massal file server dengan pelacakan perubahan.","Salah — Skrip kustom memerlukan pemeliharaan, penanganan retry, dan verifikasi integritas buatan sendiri."],"k":"Online NFS/SMB → S3 migration + scheduled incremental sync + integrity check → AWS DataSync."},{"id":"E1A-58","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"Kinesis write limits and KPL aggregation","q":"Thousands of IoT devices send readings to a Kinesis data stream with 4 provisioned shards through a fleet of producer applications. Each reading is about 100 bytes, and the producers send about 12,000 records per second in total by using individual PutRecord calls with random partition keys. Producers receive ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors even though total ingestion is only about 1.2 MB/s. The company wants to fix the throttling MOST cost-effectively without losing any readings. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Use the Kinesis Producer Library (KPL) with record aggregation so that many small readings are packed into each Kinesis record, and de-aggregate them on the consumer side with the KCL or Lambda.","Increase the stream's data retention period to 7 days.","Register every consumer as an enhanced fan-out consumer.","Change the partition key from random values to the device type."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: record kecil 'about 100 bytes', '12,000 records per second' ke '4 provisioned shards', dan total hanya 'about 1.2 MB/s'. Setiap shard menerima tulis hingga 1 MB/s atau 1.000 record/s; 4 shard hanya menerima sekitar 4.000 record/s, sehingga yang habis adalah kuota jumlah record, bukan kuota byte. KPL aggregation mengemas banyak record pengguna ke dalam satu record Kinesis, sehingga jumlah record per detik turun drastis sementara total byte tetap jauh di bawah batas; consumer berbasis KCL atau Lambda melakukan de-aggregation. Ini lebih murah daripada menambah shard tiga kali lipat hanya karena hitungan record. Distraktor terdekat adalah mengganti partition key ke device type: kardinalitas rendah justru menciptakan hot shard dan memperparah throttling. Retensi dan enhanced fan-out hanya memengaruhi penyimpanan dan sisi baca, bukan batas tulis. Aturan umum: throttling tulis Kinesis dengan banyak record kecil = batching/aggregation (KPL) sebelum menambah shard.","r":["Benar — Aggregation menurunkan jumlah record Kinesis per detik di bawah 1.000 per shard tanpa menambah shard.","Salah — Retensi hanya mengatur lama data disimpan, tidak mengubah batas tulis per shard.","Salah — Enhanced fan-out menambah throughput baca per consumer, sedangkan masalahnya ada di sisi tulis.","Salah — Partition key berkardinalitas rendah membuat hot shard dan memperburuk throttling."],"k":"Kinesis throttling tulis karena banyak record kecil (batas 1.000 record/s per shard) → KPL aggregation."},{"id":"E1C-12","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Step Functions Catch for EMR cleanup","q":"A nightly Spark job must run on a transient Amazon EMR cluster that uses a custom bootstrap action and a specific instance fleet. An AWS Step Functions workflow creates the cluster, adds the Spark step, and terminates the cluster. Last week the Spark step failed and the cluster kept running for 3 days, generating unexpected cost. Which change will prevent this with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Replace the workflow with a Lambda function that creates the cluster and terminates it after a fixed 4-hour timer.","Add a Catch on the EMR addStep.sync task that routes all errors to an EMR terminateCluster task, then to a Fail state, and also enable auto-termination on the cluster as a safety net.","Add a Retry on the addStep.sync task with MaxAttempts set to 10.","Configure a CloudWatch alarm on cluster CPU utilization that emails the team when the cluster is idle."],"a":[1],"e":"Masalahnya: saat step gagal, alur langsung berhenti sehingga task terminateCluster tidak pernah dijalankan, dan cluster terus 'kept running for 3 days'. Menambahkan Catch pada task addStep.sync agar setiap error diarahkan ke terminateCluster, lalu ke Fail state, menjamin cluster dimatikan dan eksekusi tetap tercatat gagal. Mengaktifkan auto-termination (idle timeout) EMR sebagai pengaman tambahan juga murah dan tanpa kode. Distractor terdekat adalah Retry: hanya mengulang step; jika error bersifat permanen, setelah percobaan habis cluster tetap tidak dimatikan. Lambda dengan timer tetap tidak bisa berjalan 4 jam (batas 15 menit) dan mematikan cluster yang mungkin masih bekerja. Alarm email hanya memberi tahu, tidak memperbaiki. Aturan umum: resource sementara dalam workflow perlu jalur cleanup lewat Catch (pola try/finally).","r":["Salah — Lambda tidak bisa menunggu 4 jam, dan timer tetap tidak terkait status step sebenarnya.","Benar — Catch menjamin jalur cleanup saat gagal, Fail state menjaga status eksekusi, dan auto-termination menjadi pengaman biaya.","Salah — Retry tidak membantu kegagalan permanen; setelah percobaan habis cluster tetap tidak dimatikan.","Salah — Alarm hanya memberi tahu dan masih butuh tindakan manual."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'cluster tetap jalan saat gagal' → Catch ke langkah terminate (cleanup), bukan sekadar Retry."},{"id":"E1C-49","d":1,"ts":"1.4.2","t":"Lambda reserved concurrency","q":"An AWS Lambda function loads records into an Amazon RDS for MySQL database that supports at most 100 concurrent connections. During a large backfill, the function scaled to 800 concurrent executions and the database rejected connections, which also affected other applications. The other Lambda functions in the account must not be affected by any change. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure provisioned concurrency of 100 on the function.","Increase the function memory so that each invocation finishes faster.","Configure reserved concurrency of 80 on the function.","Lower the account-level concurrency quota to 100."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya membatasi function agar tidak melebihi kapasitas koneksi database ('at most 100 concurrent connections') tanpa memengaruhi fungsi lain. Reserved concurrency menetapkan batas maksimum eksekusi bersamaan untuk satu fungsi (dan sekaligus mencadangkan kapasitas itu dari pool akun), sehingga fungsi tidak bisa melebihi 80 instance dan database tetap punya ruang untuk aplikasi lain. Distractor terdekat adalah provisioned concurrency: menyiapkan environment yang sudah hangat untuk mengurangi cold start, tetapi tidak membatasi skala maksimum fungsi. Menambah memori tidak membatasi concurrency. Menurunkan kuota akun memengaruhi semua fungsi lain. Aturan umum: lindungi downstream dengan membatasi concurrency → reserved concurrency; kurangi cold start → provisioned concurrency.","r":["Salah — Provisioned concurrency mengurangi cold start tetapi tidak membatasi jumlah eksekusi maksimum.","Salah — Fungsi masih bisa naik ke ratusan eksekusi paralel.","Benar — Reserved concurrency 80 membatasi koneksi dari fungsi ini di bawah kapasitas database tanpa mengubah fungsi lain.","Salah — Kuota akun berlaku untuk semua fungsi dan melanggar syarat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'limit Lambda to protect database' → reserved concurrency (bukan provisioned)."},{"id":"E3A-13","d":3,"ts":"3.1.4","t":"AWS Glue small file grouping","q":"An AWS Glue Spark ETL job reads about 2 million small JSON files (5 KB to 50 KB each) from Amazon S3 every hour. The script currently reads the input with spark.read.json() into a Spark DataFrame. The job is slow, and the driver sometimes fails with out-of-memory errors while listing and planning the input files. Adding more workers did not help. Which change will MOST improve the job?","o":["Change the job to an AWS Glue Python shell job.","Enable the Flex execution class for the job.","Increase the number of G.1X workers to 100.","Read the input with create_dynamic_frame.from_options and set the groupFiles option to inPartition with a suitable groupSize."],"a":[3],"e":"Petunjuknya 'millions of small files', 'driver out-of-memory saat listing', dan 'more workers did not help'. Masalah small files membuat Spark membuat satu task per file, sehingga driver kewalahan melacak jutaan task. Opsi grouping di Glue DynamicFrame (groupFiles = 'inPartition' dan groupSize) menggabungkan banyak file kecil menjadi satu grup baca, sehingga jumlah task turun drastis dan beban driver berkurang. Grouping adalah fitur pembacaan DynamicFrame (otomatis aktif bila input lebih dari 50.000 file), sehingga tidak berlaku pada spark.read.json() yang dipakai sekarang; karena itu job perlu membaca lewat create_dynamic_frame.from_options. Menambah worker tidak menolong karena bottleneck ada di driver, bukan executor. Python shell job tidak terdistribusi dan tidak cocok untuk jutaan file. Flex hanya menurunkan biaya untuk job yang tidak mendesak, tidak mempercepat. Aturan umum: banyak file kecil di Glue → aktifkan grouping (groupFiles/groupSize), dan jangka panjang lakukan compaction file ke ukuran 128 MB atau lebih.","r":["Salah — Python shell berjalan di satu mesin tanpa Spark, tidak cocok untuk volume sebesar ini.","Salah — Flex menurunkan biaya untuk job non-urgent dan tidak mengatasi masalah small files.","Salah — Bottleneck ada di driver; menambah worker tidak mengurangi jumlah task.","Benar — Membaca lewat DynamicFrame dengan grouping menggabungkan file kecil menjadi grup baca besar sehingga jumlah task dan beban driver turun."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue + 'many small files' → DynamicFrame dengan groupFiles='inPartition' + groupSize (otomatis aktif >50.000 file), atau compaction."},{"id":"E3B-34","d":3,"ts":"3.3.6","t":"AWS Glue job bookmarks","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job runs every hour and reads new files from an S3 prefix. The data engineer discovers that each run reprocesses all files in the prefix, which creates duplicate rows in the target. Which TWO actions should the engineer take so that each run processes only new files? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable job bookmarks for the job.","Ensure that the source reads in the script use a transformation_ctx parameter and that the script calls job.commit() at the end.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before every job run.","Add an AWS Glue Data Quality IsUnique rule to the job.","Increase the number of workers so that the job finishes within the hour."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'reprocesses all files' dan 'only new files'. AWS Glue job bookmarks menyimpan state data yang sudah diproses sehingga run berikutnya hanya membaca file baru. Namun bookmark baru berfungsi bila bookmark diaktifkan pada job, sumber data di script diberi transformation_ctx, dan script memanggil job.commit() agar state disimpan. Distraktor terdekat adalah aturan IsUnique Glue Data Quality: hanya mendeteksi duplikat, tidak mencegah pemrosesan ulang. Crawler memperbarui Data Catalog, bukan melacak file yang sudah diproses. Menambah worker hanya mempercepat. Aturan: incremental processing di Glue → job bookmarks + transformation_ctx + job.commit().","r":["Benar — Job bookmarks melacak data yang sudah diproses sehingga run berikutnya hanya membaca file baru.","Benar — Tanpa transformation_ctx dan job.commit(), state bookmark tidak tersimpan dan file lama akan dibaca ulang.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui skema dan partisi di Data Catalog, bukan status pemrosesan.","Salah — Aturan kualitas data mendeteksi duplikat tetapi tidak mencegah job membaca ulang file lama.","Salah — Kecepatan job tidak terkait dengan pemrosesan ulang file."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue memproses ulang data lama → job bookmarks (butuh transformation_ctx + job.commit())."},{"id":"E2B-01","d":2,"ts":"2.2.1","t":"Consuming cataloged data with Athena","q":"A retail company stores 4 TB of daily sales data as Parquet files in Amazon S3. An AWS Glue crawler has already registered the data as tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Business analysts who know SQL need to run ad hoc queries on the data a few times each week. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Launch an Amazon EMR cluster with Apache Hive, create the table definitions again in a local Hive metastore, and give the analysts access to the Hive CLI.","Use Amazon Athena to query the existing Data Catalog tables directly in Amazon S3.","Load the Parquet files into an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database each night and let the analysts query the database.","Provision an Amazon Redshift cluster and run a nightly COPY command to load all of the data before the analysts query it."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'ad hoc queries', 'a few times each week' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Datanya sudah tercatat di AWS Glue Data Catalog, sehingga Amazon Athena bisa langsung membaca skema dan lokasi S3 dari catalog tanpa memuat data ke mana pun. Athena bersifat serverless dan bayar per data yang dipindai, jadi cocok untuk query yang jarang dan tidak terjadwal. Amazon Redshift dengan COPY malam hari memang bisa, tetapi Anda harus mengelola cluster dan pipeline load untuk pemakaian yang hanya beberapa kali seminggu. EMR dengan Hive metastore lokal menduplikasi metadata yang sudah ada dan butuh pengelolaan cluster. Aturan umumnya: kalau data sudah ada di Data Catalog dan kebutuhannya SQL ad hoc atas S3, Athena adalah cara mengonsumsi data dari sumbernya dengan overhead paling kecil.","r":["Salah — EMR dengan Hive metastore lokal menduplikasi definisi tabel yang sudah ada di Data Catalog, dan Anda harus mengelola cluster.","Benar — Athena memakai Data Catalog sebagai metastore dan membaca Parquet langsung di S3 secara serverless, tanpa infrastruktur.","Salah — Memuat 4 TB per hari ke RDS menambah pipeline ETL, dan RDS tidak dirancang untuk analitik skala ini.","Salah — Redshift bisa menjalankan query ini, tetapi cluster dan load harian berlebihan untuk query ad hoc beberapa kali seminggu."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'data sudah di Glue Data Catalog' + 'SQL ad hoc' + 'least overhead' → Amazon Athena."},{"id":"E4B-26","d":4,"ts":"4.4.1","t":"CloudTrail events with EventBridge","q":"A data platform team wants to be notified within seconds when anyone calls the AWS KMS DisableKey or ScheduleKeyDeletion APIs on keys that protect the data lake, or calls the CloudTrail StopLogging API. The solution must require the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Schedule an Amazon Athena query every 24 hours against the CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 and email the results.","Create an AWS Config rule that runs every 24 hours to check whether the KMS keys are enabled.","Enable CloudTrail Insights and subscribe to Insights events.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events with these event names and sends them to an Amazon SNS topic."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'within seconds' untuk panggilan API spesifik dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Peristiwa API yang dicatat CloudTrail dikirim ke Amazon EventBridge dengan detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'; rule dengan pola eventName DisableKey, ScheduleKeyDeletion, dan StopLogging dapat langsung meneruskan ke SNS untuk notifikasi hampir real-time tanpa kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah Athena query terjadwal: datanya lengkap, tetapi delay 24 jam melanggar syarat 'within seconds'. Config rule periodik juga lambat dan hanya memeriksa status, bukan siapa yang memanggil. CloudTrail Insights mendeteksi lonjakan volume atau error rate API yang tidak biasa, bukan panggilan API tertentu. Alternatif valid lainnya adalah metric filter di CloudWatch Logs + alarm, tetapi membutuhkan trail ke CloudWatch Logs terlebih dahulu. Aturan umum: alert real-time untuk API call tertentu → EventBridge rule atas CloudTrail events.","r":["Salah — Query harian tidak memenuhi syarat notifikasi dalam hitungan detik.","Salah — Config rule periodik terlambat dan tidak memberi tahu siapa pemanggil API.","Salah — Insights mendeteksi anomali volume API, bukan memicu notifikasi untuk event name tertentu.","Benar — EventBridge rule atas CloudTrail API events mengirim notifikasi hampir real-time tanpa kode."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'notify immediately when specific API is called' → EventBridge rule (AWS API Call via CloudTrail) → SNS."},{"id":"E2C-36","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Iceberg compaction with Glue Data Catalog optimizers","q":"A company streams events through Amazon Data Firehose into an Apache Iceberg table (Parquet data files) that is registered in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Because Firehose writes frequently, the table now contains millions of small data files, and Amazon Athena queries have slowed down. The company wants a managed solution with the LEAST operational overhead. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Schedule an Amazon EMR cluster to rewrite the files every night with a custom Spark job.","Enable the automatic compaction table optimizer for the Iceberg table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog.","Increase the Athena query timeout for the workgroup.","Convert the Iceberg table back to a Hive-style table and run MSCK REPAIR TABLE."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'millions of small data files' pada tabel Iceberg dan solusi 'managed' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Glue Data Catalog menyediakan table optimizer untuk tabel Apache Iceberg, termasuk automatic compaction yang menggabungkan file kecil menjadi file yang lebih besar di latar belakang (managed compaction saat ini hanya untuk tabel Iceberg berformat Parquet, dengan strategi binpack, sort, atau Z-order), serta optimizer lain seperti snapshot retention dan orphan file deletion. File yang lebih sedikit dan lebih besar mengurangi overhead pembukaan file dan metadata sehingga query Athena lebih cepat. Job Spark kustom di EMR bisa berhasil tetapi menambah cluster dan kode yang harus dikelola. Menaikkan timeout tidak memperbaiki penyebab lambatnya query. Kembali ke tabel Hive kehilangan fitur Iceberg dan tidak menyelesaikan masalah small files. Aturan umum: small files pada Iceberg di Glue Data Catalog → aktifkan automatic compaction.","r":["Salah — Job Spark kustom di EMR berfungsi tetapi menambah infrastruktur dan pemeliharaan.","Benar — Automatic compaction Glue Data Catalog menggabungkan file kecil Iceberg secara terkelola.","Salah — Timeout lebih lama tidak mengurangi jumlah file yang harus dibaca.","Salah — Tabel Hive kehilangan fitur Iceberg dan tetap memiliki masalah small files."],"k":"Tips ujian: Iceberg small files + least overhead → Glue Data Catalog automatic compaction."},{"id":"E3A-25","d":3,"ts":"3.1.7","t":"Athena partition projection","q":"An Amazon Athena table stores application events in Amazon S3, partitioned by year, month, day, and hour. New partitions are added every hour, and the table has more than 50,000 partitions. Running MSCK REPAIR TABLE is slow, and queries spend a long time on partition metadata lookups. Which solution will improve query planning and remove the need to load partitions manually?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler every 5 minutes to add new partitions.","Configure partition projection on the table with the partition key ranges and the S3 storage location template.","Remove the partitions and store all data under a single prefix.","Convert the table to a view that unions daily tables."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'more than 50,000 partitions', 'MSCK REPAIR TABLE is slow', dan 'remove the need to load partitions manually'. Partition projection membuat Athena menghitung partisi dari konfigurasi di properti tabel (tipe, rentang nilai, dan template lokasi S3) alih-alih membaca metadata partisi dari Glue Data Catalog. Hasilnya, perencanaan query lebih cepat untuk tabel dengan sangat banyak partisi dan partisi baru langsung bisa diquery tanpa MSCK REPAIR atau ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION. Crawler setiap 5 menit menambah biaya dan tetap memakai lookup metadata yang lambat. Menghapus partisi membuat setiap query memindai semua data. View yang menggabungkan banyak tabel mempersulit pengelolaan dan tidak mengurangi pemindaian. Aturan umum: banyak partisi dengan pola yang dapat diprediksi di Athena → partition projection.","r":["Salah — Crawler berulang menambah biaya dan tidak mempercepat lookup metadata partisi.","Benar — Partition projection menghitung partisi dari konfigurasi, sehingga lebih cepat dan tanpa pemuatan partisi manual.","Salah — Tanpa partisi, setiap query memindai seluruh data sehingga lebih lambat dan mahal.","Salah — View UNION atas banyak tabel rumit dirawat dan tidak menyelesaikan masalah metadata."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena 'highly partitioned table' / 'MSCK REPAIR lambat' → partition projection."},{"id":"E3A-47","d":3,"ts":"3.2.2","t":"Verifying data with Athena","q":"Before loading a daily batch of customer records from Amazon S3 into Amazon Redshift, a data engineer must verify that customer_id has no duplicates and that the email column has no null values. The data is already cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. The engineer wants to run the checks in place without provisioning any infrastructure. Which approach meets these requirements?","o":["Load the batch into Amazon Redshift first, then check for duplicates and nulls and delete bad rows.","Run Amazon Athena queries on the cataloged table, such as SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) FROM t GROUP BY customer_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1, and SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t WHERE email IS NULL.","Launch an Amazon EMR cluster and run a Spark job that counts duplicates and nulls.","Download the files and inspect them manually in a text editor."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'verify before loading', 'run the checks in place', dan 'without provisioning any infrastructure'. Amazon Athena bersifat serverless dan bisa langsung meng-query data di S3 melalui tabel di Glue Data Catalog. Query GROUP BY dengan HAVING COUNT(*) > 1 menemukan duplikat, dan filter IS NULL menghitung nilai yang hilang. Hasilnya bisa dipakai sebagai gerbang sebelum proses load. Memuat ke Redshift dulu melanggar syarat 'before loading' dan berisiko mencemari warehouse. Cluster EMR adalah infrastruktur yang harus disediakan. Pemeriksaan manual tidak skalabel dan rawan salah. Aturan umum: validasi data ad hoc langsung di S3 tanpa infrastruktur → Athena SQL.","r":["Salah — Melanggar syarat validasi sebelum load dan bisa mencemari tabel produksi.","Benar — Athena serverless memeriksa duplikat dan null langsung di S3 dengan SQL sederhana.","Salah — EMR membutuhkan penyediaan dan pengelolaan cluster.","Salah — Pemeriksaan manual tidak skalabel dan tidak bisa diandalkan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'verify data in S3 in place, serverless' → Athena (GROUP BY ... HAVING COUNT(*) > 1, IS NULL)."},{"id":"E1B-06","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Serverless Spark options","q":"A data engineering team has dozens of existing PySpark scripts that currently run on a self-managed Spark cluster. The team wants to move the scripts to AWS with minimal code changes and without provisioning, patching, or sizing any cluster nodes. Which TWO services meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Amazon EMR on Amazon EC2 with managed scaling","AWS Glue ETL jobs","AWS Lambda functions packaged as container images with PySpark","Amazon EMR Serverless","Amazon Redshift stored procedures"],"a":[1,3],"e":"Syarat utamanya adalah 'minimal code changes' untuk skrip PySpark dan 'without provisioning, patching, or sizing any cluster nodes'. AWS Glue ETL job dan Amazon EMR Serverless sama-sama menjalankan Apache Spark secara serverless: Anda cukup mengirim skrip, dan AWS mengelola kapasitas worker. EMR on EC2 dengan managed scaling adalah distraktor terdekat karena scaling-nya otomatis, tetapi Anda tetap memilih instance type, mengelola cluster, dan menangani patch AMI. Lambda tidak cocok untuk Spark terdistribusi karena batas 15 menit dan satu lingkungan eksekusi tunggal. Redshift stored procedure menuntut penulisan ulang ke SQL. Aturan umum: Spark tanpa mengelola cluster → AWS Glue atau EMR Serverless.","r":["Salah — Managed scaling mengatur jumlah node, tetapi cluster EC2 tetap harus diprovisi, dipilih instance-nya, dan dikelola.","Benar — Glue menjalankan PySpark secara serverless dengan perubahan kode minimal.","Salah — Lambda bukan lingkungan Spark terdistribusi dan dibatasi 15 menit serta memori 10 GB.","Benar — EMR Serverless menjalankan job Spark tanpa provisioning atau pengelolaan cluster.","Salah — Membutuhkan penulisan ulang logika PySpark menjadi SQL."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'run Spark without managing clusters' → AWS Glue atau Amazon EMR Serverless."},{"id":"E3B-24","d":3,"ts":"3.3.7","t":"Lambda logging configuration","q":"A data team runs 60 Python AWS Lambda functions that use the standard logging library. In production, the functions produce very large volumes of DEBUG and INFO logs, and the team wants machine-parsable logs for CloudWatch Logs Insights. The team wants to change behavior through configuration rather than by editing each function's code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Set a 1-day retention policy on every Lambda log group.","Create a subscription filter that drops DEBUG and INFO events before they are stored.","Disable CloudWatch Logs permissions in the functions' execution role.","Use Lambda advanced logging controls to set the log format to JSON and the application log level to WARN for each function."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'machine-parsable', 'reduce DEBUG and INFO', dan 'through configuration rather than code'. Lambda advanced logging controls memungkinkan pengaturan log format JSON serta filter application log level dan system log level per fungsi, sehingga log di bawah WARN tidak dikirim ke CloudWatch Logs dan log menjadi terstruktur untuk Logs Insights; ini berlaku untuk runtime yang menggunakan library logging standar. Distraktor terdekat adalah subscription filter — subscription filter hanya meneruskan salinan event ke tujuan lain, tidak mencegah event disimpan di log group. Retensi 1 hari mengurangi penyimpanan tetapi tetap membayar ingestion dan menghilangkan log penting. Mencabut izin log menghilangkan semua log. Aturan: kontrol level dan format log Lambda tanpa ubah kode → advanced logging controls.","r":["Salah — Biaya ingestion tetap terjadi dan log penting ikut hilang setelah 1 hari.","Salah — Subscription filter hanya menyalin event ke tujuan lain; event tetap tersimpan di log group.","Salah — Mematikan semua log merusak kemampuan troubleshooting dan audit.","Benar — Advanced logging controls mengatur format JSON dan level log minimum per fungsi lewat konfigurasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda JSON logs / log level tanpa ubah kode → Lambda advanced logging controls."},{"id":"E1A-01","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"Kinesis Data Streams vs Data Firehose","q":"A retail company streams website clickstream events at about 20 MB/s. Three independent applications (fraud detection, personalization, and a real-time dashboard) must each read every event within 1 second of arrival, and events for the same user must be processed in order. Which ingestion solution meets these requirements?","o":["Send the events to Amazon Data Firehose and configure three delivery destinations on the same Firehose stream.","Send the events to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams with the user ID as the partition key, and have each application consume the stream independently.","Send the events to an Amazon SQS standard queue and have the three applications poll the same queue.","Write the events to Amazon S3 and configure S3 Event Notifications to invoke each application."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci penentunya adalah 'three independent applications must each read every event', 'within 1 second', dan 'in order' per user. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams (KDS) menyimpan record di shard sehingga banyak consumer bisa membaca data yang sama secara independen dengan latensi sub-detik. Dengan partition key = user ID, semua event dari user yang sama masuk ke shard yang sama sehingga urutannya terjaga. Distraktor terdekat adalah Data Firehose, tetapi satu Firehose stream hanya punya satu destination dan dirancang untuk delivery dengan buffering (bukan multi-consumer sub-detik). SQS standard tidak menjamin urutan dan setiap pesan hanya diproses oleh satu consumer. Aturan umum: banyak consumer + replay + ordering per key + latensi rendah = Kinesis Data Streams.","r":["Salah — Satu Firehose stream hanya mengirim ke satu destination dan bukan stream multi-consumer; bahkan dengan zero buffering, delivery tetap butuh beberapa detik.","Benar — KDS mendukung banyak consumer independen dengan latensi sub-detik, dan partition key user ID menjaga urutan per user.","Salah — SQS standard tidak menjamin urutan, dan pesan yang sudah diambil satu consumer tidak dibaca utuh oleh consumer lain.","Salah — Menulis ke S3 dulu lalu memicu event menambah latensi dan tidak menjamin urutan per user."],"k":"Multiple independent consumers + ordering per key + sub-second → Kinesis Data Streams (partition key = entity ID)."},{"id":"E2C-02","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Redshift sort keys and zone maps","q":"A data engineer manages an Amazon Redshift table that stores 3 years of clickstream events. More than 90% of dashboard queries filter on a narrow range of event_date (for example, the last 7 days), and new data is loaded daily in event_date order. Query performance has degraded as the table has grown. Which design change will MOST improve the performance of these queries?","o":["Change the distribution style of the table to DISTSTYLE ALL.","Define event_date as the leading column of a compound sort key.","Create a late-binding view over the table that filters on event_date.","Increase the column compression on event_date to ZSTD."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'filter on a narrow range of event_date' dan data dimuat berurutan berdasarkan tanggal. Di Amazon Redshift, sort key menentukan urutan fisik data di disk, dan zone maps (nilai min/max per blok) memungkinkan Redshift melewati blok yang tidak relevan dengan range filter. Compound sort key dengan event_date sebagai kolom pertama sangat efektif untuk range filter dan cocok dengan pola load yang sudah berurutan sehingga kebutuhan VACUUM sort kecil. DISTSTYLE ALL untuk tabel clickstream besar justru memperbesar storage dan tidak mengurangi blok yang dipindai. View hanya membungkus query dan tidak mengubah cara data disimpan. Mengganti encoding hanya mengurangi ukuran data, bukan jumlah blok yang harus dipindai berdasarkan filter. Aturan umum: kolom yang paling sering dipakai pada range filter (biasanya timestamp) adalah kandidat utama sort key.","r":["Salah — DISTSTYLE ALL menyalin tabel besar ke setiap node; tidak membantu range filter dan menambah biaya storage.","Benar — Compound sort key dengan event_date di depan memungkinkan zone maps melewati blok di luar range tanggal.","Salah — View tidak mengubah layout fisik data sehingga jumlah blok yang dipindai tetap sama.","Salah — Encoding mengecilkan ukuran kolom, tetapi tanpa sort key Redshift tetap memindai hampir semua blok."],"k":"Tips ujian: query sering filter range tanggal di Redshift → jadikan kolom tanggal sebagai (leading) sort key."},{"id":"E1C-36","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"SNS to SQS fan-out","q":"When a curated dataset is published, three downstream systems must be notified: a Redshift loader, a search indexer, and an ML feature pipeline. Each consumer processes at its own pace, must not lose notifications if it is temporarily down, and must be able to retry independently. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Publish the notification to a single Amazon SQS queue that all three consumers poll.","Publish the notification to an Amazon SNS topic and have each consumer subscribe with its own email endpoint.","Invoke the three consumers' Lambda functions synchronously, one after another, from the publishing job.","Publish the notification to an Amazon SNS topic that has three Amazon SQS queues subscribed, one for each consumer."],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhannya: tiga konsumen, 'each consumer processes at its own pace', 'must not lose notifications if ... temporarily down', dan 'retry independently'. Pola fan-out SNS ke SQS mengirim salinan pesan ke setiap antrean; tiap antrean menyimpan pesan secara tahan lama hingga konsumennya siap, dan setiap konsumen memiliki visibility timeout serta DLQ sendiri. Distractor terdekat adalah satu antrean SQS bersama: setiap pesan hanya dikonsumsi oleh satu konsumen, sehingga dua sistem lain tidak menerima notifikasi. Endpoint email tidak bisa diproses oleh sistem secara andal. Pemanggilan sinkron berurutan membuat publisher bergantung pada ketersediaan semua konsumen. Aturan umum: satu event ke banyak konsumen yang independen dan tahan lama → SNS fan-out ke beberapa SQS queue.","r":["Salah — Pada satu antrean, setiap pesan hanya diterima oleh satu konsumen.","Salah — Email tidak cocok sebagai integrasi antar sistem dan tidak bisa di-retry otomatis.","Salah — Publisher terikat pada ketersediaan setiap konsumen dan kegagalan satu konsumen memengaruhi lainnya.","Benar — Fan-out SNS ke SQS memberi setiap konsumen salinan pesan yang tahan lama dan retry independen."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'multiple independent consumers' + 'durable' → SNS fan-out to SQS queues."}]});